   215	- **The three papers.** (1) **The records:** a seat-courier's flat of waxed leather; six taped rows, a year to a row, of survey abstracts measured in lengths, knots and strides, with the dead surveyor's four-sign index printed at their heads; an **anomaly column** in which every sheet, in every hand, for six years carries the one word *Total* (an entry, not a sum; no figure); "More than four" (Karis, counting distinct sign-groups; she gives no number); the Fallow completion report is the last, loose sheet, and carries **five strokes for a name and a count of six** (locked Book 7 ch40, ch43), not five names. (2) **The page:** a COPY in Vastin's own hand of one line from an old register, carried in oilcloth in his coat: "—of the Architect: see the lower archive at Treswick, which holds it in full—". "The Architect" is a title, not a name, and a word Karis has never met in any stratum. It is never called a leaf; **the leaf has not appeared**. (3) **The technician's sheet:** the two protected lines with a date between them, a brush bar across what followed, and Karis's *not read*. **The date is a Compact date, a registry year and a day in it, and is never printed as figures** (the source gives none; no owner decision is needed). The office had filed the sheet at the end of the second row and it lies there again.
