    15	## Decisions made before drafting
    16	
    17	1. **West is a job.** Cael rules on a slip and says so: he can price a cut, and he will not vow a town. The boxes and the papers come because nothing of theirs is left in a store. Nobody votes on the town.
    18	2. **The rope is not bought.** The broker's cordage is three-strand. Brom will not pay a debt in a rope that was not asked for. The purse stays at 118 until the factor pays; the debt stands.
    19	3. **Deployment moves to thirty-two** on the 279th: one Ember point at the mark (the one who is meant to be loud), and one Wind burst, away. Nothing else is opened. No eleventh comes.
    20	4. **The technician's date is never printed.** The office that keeps the stations opens its year on a different day from the seat's registry, so a station's "year and day" must be turned before it can be laid beside a registry date; Vastin gives the difference while reading the abstracts for procedure, and the page does not give the number. Cael turns it and comes out on the date that has stood at the head of his own file on every desk since his Kindling. No span is computed. He does not write it.
    21	5. **The short count has a cause.** Seln has drawn the technician's sheet out of the second row to do the turn in daylight; Karis then hands that row to Cael to be counted a second time. It comes out one under her figure. No figures for the rows are printed.
