    41	He left them, and Cael looked along the meadow, where seven fires were burning now for the three of the last snow. The carts had begun to come down, off the north water and over the saddle, and each of them drew up along the river with its shafts lowered and a stone behind every wheel, to wait for the same boat as everybody else. The hide-woman had a neighbour at last, a man with a string of nine mules who had pitched within a yard of her and been told what she thought of it.
    42	
