   217	Cael walked by the three carts. He had not meant to look at them, and he looked: a wheel with two spokes gone, and a barrel-head with a hold's mark burned in it, and under the nearest bed a mule's collar, with the straw coming out. Somebody had driven that cart for two days up a silent road with a Path in his pocket. He had kept it there until the very last hundred strides.
   218	
   219	Karis stopped there, at the bank's end, with the mule's cheek-strap in one hand and Hesk's clock in the other. Oryn stood beside her with her arms bare to the elbow. Neither of them said anything, since there was nothing that the road allowed.
