   223	At sixty strides there was a flat stone at the road's edge, and Brom stepped onto it and set his feet, with the rock held against his thigh. Vastin stopped behind him. Cael did not see where Lira went; there was a small dry rattle on the scree above, and then nothing. Seln had left them at the foot, and was already nowhere.
