   242	
   243	They came over the north bank at the mark, as Lira had said that they would, and he turned his head as far as a post may. There were five, grey and long, pouring over the worn places with their heads level. And behind those, out from under the strip that nobody had been able to see, there came three more.
   244	
   245	He was two strides from Brom's stone. He stopped, and stood, and counted eight.
   246	
   247	They reached the tow, where there was a smear of soot on the ice and nothing else. He waited for them to stand.
   248	
