   239	He had a good deal to carry besides the box, and he went over it, a stride at a time, as he would have gone over a count. There was a job, done and paid, with a hundred and thirty-eight marks to show for it. There was a wall that he had stood behind for the space of one count, and an eleventh thing that had not come of it. There was a mark in a small ruled square, which was on five sheets and an iron stake and which nobody could read. He had a name, short and strange, for a man who sat under a town. He had two sentences in a book, in his own hand, about a flight of steps and a paved place.
