   441	- **C4 — The grandmother.** The universe ledger lists "Hesk's grandmother" as the owner of the straightedge saying. Book 7 edition chapter 60's note (chapter-60.md:67) [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 11] ("Your grandmother said…") and S17/S24 make her **Cael's** grandmother, Hesk's late wife. **Edition follows the prose.** The ledger line is a slip.
   442	- **C5 — Rune's tier.** The universe bible says "Cael's twelfth (Rune-adjacent, partial, Bronze)". The notice says "Rune family … Tier equivalent unknown". **Edition follows the notice.** Bronze is Cleon's tier.
   443	- **C6 — Architecture residue.** The architecture's header, plant ledger and checkpoint still say Cael turns twenty in Ch14, the terminus is "the Still Court", and there is a "sixth" site. **Superseded** by rulings 12 and 13 and by the closed prose: nineteen throughout, "the court", the fifth.
   444	- **C7 — Reveal locus.** CANON_RULES says "ancient records in edge-territory ruins"; the bible says a "pre-Compact archive at a border city". The source stages both: the leaf is in the Treswick archive and its key is the ruins' carvings. **Flag for the bible pass.**
   445	- **C8 — Fragment trajectory.** The bible's "22 integrations by Book 10" leaves nine for Book 9 and the Book 10 skip. DECISIONS row 11 left this OPEN with a proposal (≈17 by Book 10, 22 by Book 11). **Not Book 8's to settle.** Book 9's planner must plan the rate and say so.
FILE:editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md
     1	# Movement brief 005 — No Authority
     2	
     3	- PWA book id: fractured-path/book-08-before-the-paths (Monroe 1.3 edition)
     4	- Series id: fractured-path
     5	- Author: Opus (Claude Opus 5.5)
     6	- Chapters: 27–33 (7 chapters) → `manuscript/chapter-27.md` … `chapter-33.md`
     7	- Word budget: ~35,000
     8	- Owner names: no new names. The broker's factor and the six attackers stay faceless and unnamed.
     9	
    10	> **[Coordinator rulings after the Movement 1 audit, 2026-10-11 — binding; they override any plan text below that differs.]** (1) **Teague's spear is a tall MAN** (he / him): the locked Book 7 wrote him so (ch25, ch51, ch52), and Book 8 follows its own edition (OWNER-pending #59). Where the plan says "the tall woman", read "the tall man"; his silence toward the six until his question at the pass stands. (2) **Teague can read** (locked Book 7 ch25: he read a slip twice). Never write that he cannot; if he does not read a sheet it is because it is not in front of him or he has no need. (3) **Lira's asking:** she asked Oryn once about the ankle on the mountain in Book 7 and asked nobody for anything from then until Thornwater; do not call Thornwater her first ask since Norhold. (4) **The stroke and bar** is on stake thirty-two (the Stair's newer stake and the kit's unused one) and on the fourth site's thirty-four ONLY; stakes thirty-one and thirty-three do not carry it. Later records may show the grade on survey SHEETS; the field stakes do not all carry it. (5) **The cord:** the kit's cord is twenty strides, knotted at the fives (four knots to a length); Book 7's Ring was sixty-two cords and twenty strides round. The court is about 1,107 yards across, which is about FIFTY cords, not 159. Give no yardage for a cord. (6) **"West"** was first said aloud at the six-person table on the 268th (Karis's protected "It's west… Treswick…" speech, printed once in ch6). (7) **Deployment since the Line is twenty-nine** at the end of Movement 1 (two uses of the Iron read in earnest); trials are not counted.
    11	
    12	> **[Coordinator rulings after the Movement 2 audit, 2026-10-11 — binding; they override any plan text below that differs.]** (1) **Vastin's second paper is "the page": a COPY in his own hand** of one line from an old register ("—of the Architect: see the lower archive at Treswick, which holds it in full—"). It was never cut from anything and is never called a leaf; "the leaf" is the chamber record of Movement 6 only. (2) **The technician's sheet carries a Compact date (a registry year and a day in it) that is NEVER printed as figures** anywhere in this book; whoever reads it reads a date, and the page does not give its numbers. The office filed that sheet at the end of the second row of the records, and it lies there. (3) **The anomaly column:** on every survey abstract, in every hand, for six years, the entry is the one word *Total* — an entry, not a sum. (4) **The Fallow completion report** carries five strokes for a name and a count of six (locked Book 7), not five written names. (5) **What Vastin has told the six about the layer is four things only:** no key (it cannot be reached); the citation; the suppressed records; the technician's line. He has not defined "classification event" and does not know which event is meant. Nothing on the page says that menders, technicians or any office have tried to open it or know more. (6) **Speakers:** "What follows you," was Lira's; "She's right. Go and lie down, and don't take the stairs fast," was Oryn's. (7) **Deployment since the Line is thirty** at the end of Movement 2 (the Iron read at the landing on the 277th). Purse 118 marks. (8) **Teague's spear** has "he/his" on the page from chapter 7 (OWNER-pending #59 as defaulted). (9) Vastin has shown no Iron Wall, has no stated age, has asked only for a bed, and holds Karis's unsealed receipt. Cael has not touched the page and has not read the sheet's date closely.
    13	
    14	> **[Coordinator note 2026-10-11 — NO-SOURCE drafting, binding.]** Draft WITHOUT opening any source chapter under `books/`. The source-chapter references in the line below are retained for the coordinator's and reviewers' tools only; the author does not read them. Events come from this packet, `BOOK_MAP.md` (the plan sections, the protected-text section and the reserved-truths section) and `STATE_LEDGER.md`. Write `EVENT-LIST.md` first. Where a protected unit is quoted in the plan only in part, leave `[[TIER-B: <unit> — coordinator to supply protected text]]` and write around it. [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 1]
    15	
    16	- Read before drafting:
    17	  - Source `chapter-10.md`, `chapter-11.md` and `chapter-12.md`.
    18	  - The previous ending is this edition's `manuscript/chapter-26.md`.
    19	  - From `BOOK_MAP.md`: §2 items 19–22; §3 A (the alley), B 3–4; §5 (the Seln and Karis cutaways); §7.1 (Iron Wall, Rune Path); §8 (the alley); §10 (Tier A 9, 12; S10–S12 lines); §12 C2; §13.
    20	  - `STATE_LEDGER.md`, latest section.
    21	
    22	## Where we enter
    23	
    24	It is the 284th day, under Treswick. The lamp goes into the middle gallery. A light is already on at its end, and a man is already reading.
    25	
    26	## What this movement is for
    27	
    28	This is the archive's first week. Karis has found the room she has wanted all her life. A marshal learns his name is a blade with no handle. A craftsman shows how he reads a made thing's bones. Brom is offered the life his family wanted and picks up a box. Seln looks at the door his old trade would have used and decides nothing. Then the faction reaches inside the walls. A man with nothing behind him holds a line for people the Compact would restrict, and Cael comes away with the eleventh. We cross the first third into the middle, and progression language surfaces at the turning points: Rune explained, Iron Wall paid, the notice.
    29	
    30	Consequential turns and promises:
    31	- **The Deepstacks (284th).** The galleries, the shelving, the smell of a place where nothing has been decided. Cleon reads to the end of his page first. The sheets are laid out 11/29/12. Karis: "Older than [UNBOUND]." Cleon: "I know that hand." "Being believed … It's the end of being able to be wrong." "Give me a week." Cael finds himself, for the first time, unfiled.
    32	- **The yard door (285th).** Vastin's reflex: "Vastin. Archmarshal, Compact enforcement. You'll find the name is —". **Seln answers truthfully** (ruling 25): "He's on the count … the form asks what a hand's for, not what he was." The narration records that Seln did not lie and what not lying cost him. "I'm sorry." / "Don't be sorry. Be nobody." Cael's fellow-feeling on the landing. **The log, verbatim.**
    33	- **The chamber days (285th–289th; ~8,000 on the page, including the 288th–289th the source left undramatized).**
    34	  - The lamp trade: a hand to the left of the line.
    35	  - Cleon's board against the Hall's fourth sheet: bearer, carried, ornament. "They're orders." **The limit, verbatim.** "Same make."
    36	  - Cael wants the instrument turned on himself, notes the wish and does not say it.
    37	  - The decipherment's first steps: the board's numerals, then the first letters arriving from the three floors.
    38	  - **Vastin learning to be nobody**, badly. He moves toward the lamp four times on the fourth day. "How long did it take you." / "I was fourteen. I'm nineteen. I'm not there yet either."
    39	- **Brom's yard (~2,000).** He rights a broker's cart with his back and no Path, spending the good shoulder. The broker offers a guard's post, a pass and a bed inside the second wall. "I'll think on it." He picks up the box on the bound shoulder, a debt Cael enters. On the stair: "You think Karis is right?" … "Good. I'd hate to have turned down a real job for a wrong hunch."
    40	- **Seln's night walk.** Cael hears the room change shape. From a roof below the walls Seln looks at the registry and the station's light. "I looked at it." It is six words in the morning log.
    41	- **Cleon's close (287th), verbatim:** "documentation … built the same way twice … never once slept well since."
    42	- **The alley (290th dusk; ~4,000, developed).** Staging follows BOOK_MAP §8. Vastin turns uphill and roots the cut wall to wall: "there is no round." Nobody declares. Brom with a loose step-stone. Lira's drop, the knife into the stave's shaft. Cael stands still at the plane's foot for a minute and some, as "the reason". Seln's weighted cord from the roof takes the signaller. The cache was on the roof the whole time. They leave: none taken, no faces, nobody dead.
    43	- **Costs and the acquisition.** Karis's left hand is cut on a step's edge. Brom binds it with thread, a strip of shirt and his teeth, because no healer inside the gate would put hands on it. Vastin is spent past the road and the knee goes again. **The Iron-Wall notice renders, verbatim.** "I put the wall in front of it anyway. I'd like that entered" / "It's entered." **Not told.** The faction's limit is entered as a finding. **The log, verbatim.**
    44	
    45	**Physical challenge:** the alley (a major fight) and Brom's cart.
    46	**Cutaways (~4,500):** Seln, ~2,000, on the night walk: the roof, the locked case's weight [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 23], the registry's door, deciding nothing. **The contents stay unknown.** Karis, ~2,500, in the decipherment: her method, her refusal to guess, the letters coming one by one. **The leaf is not readable in this movement.**
    47	**Development:** about 15 Cael beats. Supporting: Vastin 3, Brom 2, Seln 2, Karis 2, Cleon 2, Lira 1.
    48	
    49	## What must remain true / withheld
    50	
    51	- Cleon's Path is shown from outside only. The *inside* (the lean) and the acquisition belong to Movement 6. **No twelfth here.**
    52	- The eleventh is acquired in the alley's quiet middle minute, after Iron Wall has been witnessed in use: the cut first, then this full minute. It is **not deployed and not told** to Vastin.
    53	- Karis does not read the leaf yet. The bundle is on Cleon's shelf, a thing with a lean and no language.
    54	- The faction expected a declaration and saw a wall and a rock in an alley. **It sees nothing of quiet ground.**
    55	- No healer works inside the gate. Oryn is north.
    56	- Vastin does not know the mechanism and his age is not stated. "Forty years" is his rounding.
    57	
    58	## What the author owns
    59	
    60	The galleries' geography. The order of the chamber days, and which small discoveries Karis makes on which day. Brom's yard and the broker's words. How the alley's minute feels from two feet below a plane. Where the humour sits: the lamp, the chairs with and without cushions, Brom's "Cart was heavier".
    61	
    62	## Where we leave pressure
    63	
    64	The faction knows where they sleep, and they know the crew knows it. A man who held a wall for them has asked for it to be entered, and Cael has entered more than the man knows. Karis has three days left of Cleon's week. A board leans, and a boy holding a lamp has started to notice which way.
