     1	# Movement brief 006 — Before the Paths
     2	
     3	- PWA book id: fractured-path/book-08-before-the-paths (Monroe 1.3 edition)
     4	- Series id: fractured-path
     5	- Author: Opus (Claude Opus 5.5)
     6	- Chapters: 34–40 (7 chapters) → `manuscript/chapter-34.md` … `chapter-40.md`
     7	- Word budget: ~34,000
     8	- Owner names: no new names. The hood in the tail stays faceless. The hold child in Oryn's cutaway stays unnamed.
     9	
    10	> **[Coordinator rulings after the Movement 1 audit, 2026-10-11 — binding; they override any plan text below that differs.]** (1) **Teague's spear is a tall MAN** (he / him): the locked Book 7 wrote him so (ch25, ch51, ch52), and Book 8 follows its own edition (OWNER-pending #59). Where the plan says "the tall woman", read "the tall man"; his silence toward the six until his question at the pass stands. (2) **Teague can read** (locked Book 7 ch25: he read a slip twice). Never write that he cannot; if he does not read a sheet it is because it is not in front of him or he has no need. (3) **Lira's asking:** she asked Oryn once about the ankle on the mountain in Book 7 and asked nobody for anything from then until Thornwater; do not call Thornwater her first ask since Norhold. (4) **The stroke and bar** is on stake thirty-two (the Stair's newer stake and the kit's unused one) and on the fourth site's thirty-four ONLY; stakes thirty-one and thirty-three do not carry it. Later records may show the grade on survey SHEETS; the field stakes do not all carry it. (5) **The cord:** the kit's cord is twenty strides, knotted at the fives (four knots to a length); Book 7's Ring was sixty-two cords and twenty strides round. The court is about 1,107 yards across, which is about FIFTY cords, not 159. Give no yardage for a cord. (6) **"West"** was first said aloud at the six-person table on the 268th (Karis's protected "It's west… Treswick…" speech, printed once in ch6). (7) **Deployment since the Line is twenty-nine** at the end of Movement 1 (two uses of the Iron read in earnest); trials are not counted.
    11	
    12	> **[Coordinator rulings after the Movement 2 audit, 2026-10-11 — binding; they override any plan text below that differs.]** (1) **Vastin's second paper is "the page": a COPY in his own hand** of one line from an old register ("—of the Architect: see the lower archive at Treswick, which holds it in full—"). It was never cut from anything and is never called a leaf; "the leaf" is the chamber record of Movement 6 only. (2) **The technician's sheet carries a Compact date (a registry year and a day in it) that is NEVER printed as figures** anywhere in this book; whoever reads it reads a date, and the page does not give its numbers. The office filed that sheet at the end of the second row of the records, and it lies there. (3) **The anomaly column:** on every survey abstract, in every hand, for six years, the entry is the one word *Total* — an entry, not a sum. (4) **The Fallow completion report** carries five strokes for a name and a count of six (locked Book 7), not five written names. (5) **What Vastin has told the six about the layer is four things only:** no key (it cannot be reached); the citation; the suppressed records; the technician's line. He has not defined "classification event" and does not know which event is meant. Nothing on the page says that menders, technicians or any office have tried to open it or know more. (6) **Speakers:** "What follows you," was Lira's; "She's right. Go and lie down, and don't take the stairs fast," was Oryn's. (7) **Deployment since the Line is thirty** at the end of Movement 2 (the Iron read at the landing on the 277th). Purse 118 marks. (8) **Teague's spear** has "he/his" on the page from chapter 7 (OWNER-pending #59 as defaulted). (9) Vastin has shown no Iron Wall, has no stated age, has asked only for a bed, and holds Karis's unsealed receipt. Cael has not touched the page and has not read the sheet's date closely.
    13	
    14	> **[Coordinator note 2026-10-11 — NO-SOURCE drafting, binding.]** Draft WITHOUT opening any source chapter under `books/`. The source-chapter references in the line below are retained for the coordinator's and reviewers' tools only; the author does not read them. Events come from this packet, `BOOK_MAP.md` (the plan sections, the protected-text section and the reserved-truths section) and `STATE_LEDGER.md`. Write `EVENT-LIST.md` first. Where a protected unit is quoted in the plan only in part, leave `[[TIER-B: <unit> — coordinator to supply protected text]]` and write around it. [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 1]
    15	
    16	- Read before drafting:
    17	  - Source `chapter-13.md`, `chapter-14.md`, `chapter-15.md` and `chapter-16.md`. Read `chapter-15.md` twice.
    18	  - The previous ending is this edition's `manuscript/chapter-33.md`.
    19	  - From `BOOK_MAP.md`: §2 items 23–26; §3 A (the tail), B 5; §5 (the Vastin and Oryn cutaways); §7.1 (Rune; the instruments); **§9 (all of it)**; §10 Tier A 1–3, 10, 13, 15, 17–18 and the S13–S16 Tier C lines; **§11**; §12 C10; §13.
    20	  - `STATE_LEDGER.md`, latest section.
    21	
    22	## Where we enter
    23	
    24	It is the 291st day. After the alley the working party goes by the carts' street in daylight, with the boxes on a borrowed handcart. Karis's left hand is bound in a strip of Brom's shirt. Cael has eleven fragments and the eleventh has nothing to do. The clerk has not asked three things.
    25	
    26	## What this movement is for
    27	
    28	This movement holds the book's reveal and the arc's second pole. The twelfth arrives at a word and carries a warning. A parcel brings the second half of a competence, and the largest instrument on the continent does a wrong thing once, for him. Then the leaf is read aloud **once**, and that night Cael takes it on his feet: not excluded but *prevented*, and he happened anyway. **This is a deliberately quiet movement, with one set piece.** The reason is that the reveal must land as a discovery on paper by a researcher, and the fire must hold. The physical pressure is the tail chase and the faction's presence in the streets.
    29	
    30	Consequential turns and promises:
    31	- **The reader (291st).** Cleon shows the Path from inside: "A record sits … An instruction *leans* … This is a stair." Karis: "The strata lean too." Then **the acquisition at "there"**. The fifth row leans, and so does the board, and Cael does not turn the twelfth on anything else. He tells Lira first on the stair ("Twelfth. His. Lean."), then goes back down and tells Cleon at the bell, in the order he has it. "You did what." "That's not in the classification system. That's not *supposed* to be possible. That's —" / "No. I'll not say that one." The cup of water, and **the warning, verbatim**. "He went back to the carving." Vastin and Cael carry the case up the stair together. **The notice on the stair, verbatim**, with *He looked away. Kept.* The eyes are paid on the last flight. **"Cael did not tell anyone. He remembered."**
    32	- **Rune practice (~2,000, folded across the days).** The twelfth leans at every made thing: the inn table's joints, the bridge's arches, the dividers' hinge. He learns not to look, as he learned not to look at the light. It is never used on a person.
    33	- **The tail (291st–292nd night; ~2,500 set piece).** Seln and Cael follow a hood through the outer district. The hood goes through a tier gate Cael cannot legally cross, and he stops at the line. No faces, none taken, nothing learned but the faction's patience.
    34	- **Dividers (292nd).** The parcel and **Hesk's note, verbatim**. The meal: four marks, two cups kept, and Seln's slip read and burned ("Closed"), leaving 130. Vastin and the cups: "Out here you count who's owed a seat." This is **the first inventory written inside walls** (§12 C10). **The light, not steady for a count of one:** "an instrument turning toward him." It is the fourth entry on the page. He does not cross. The promise holds at its first cost.
    35	- **The leaf (293rd morning).** Describe the object before the reading: horn-coloured, point-written, the scraped name with its first upright stroke. Karis reads it **aloud once** (§9; §10 Tier A 1), then paraphrases it once: "the Architect" is a title, about four hundred years ago, and the purpose is the un-bound. "Older. Made. Us." Cael catalogues the room, not himself. **The chronicle** is marked: "Marked." / "Marked." Vastin reaches ("the mark that is given at the kindling —") and Karis answers with **two pages** and the ruler rule. The copy, with the gap drawn.
    36	- **The yard fire (293rd evening).** Seln is told on the street ("Made." "For a kind."). Cleon comes up, the only time. Cael gives **Lira the page to read first**; nobody explains it to her. "So the whole time they weren't afraid you'd break something. They were afraid you'd *exist*." Brom prices it. Seln will keep the cache "a while longer". Karis says two pages, then sleeps on a bucket. Brom to Cleon: "Good." Vastin: "aimed … At a category. Which turned out to be a person. Who's sitting across the fire." Lira: "You signed the mark at kindlings." / "I would have." **Pole two**, taken on his feet and not catalogued, verbatim. "I want to stand in the middle of it." Cleon leaves: "Tomorrow the rest of the leaf. The list of parts."
    37	
    38	**Physical challenge:** the tail (set piece). The eyes' cost on the stair.
    39	**Cutaways (~4,500):** Vastin, ~2,000, alone after the leaf. "Aimed." His sentence stays stopped in his head too. **He does not join the leaf to the sigils, does no date arithmetic, and names no seals.** Oryn, ~2,500, at a hold on her route, where a fourteen-year-old's Kindling happens. She watches a child see a sigil nobody else can see, and thinks of a dark one. **She has not heard the leaf. Nobody dies.**
    40	**Development:** about 16 Cael beats (the middle-third bump). Supporting: Lira 2, Karis 2, Cleon 2, Vastin 2, Seln 1–2, Brom 1, Oryn 1.
    41	
    42	## What must remain true / withheld
    43	
    44	- **The reveal is spoken once.** "Four hundred years" appears only in the record's voice, in Karis's single paraphrase, and in Cael's pole-two sentence. "The Architect" is a title, never an agent.
    45	- **There is no line between the leaf and the sigils**, anywhere, in any head. Never use *terminal*, *circuit* or *infrastructure*.
    46	- The chronicle's hole stays a hole. Book 11's plant is marked, not read.
    47	- The twelfth is not turned on Cael's own still place in this movement. It does not turn unbidden until Millrace (Movement 7).
    48	- The light is deniable. Nothing hints at agency. Nineteen, and **no birthday**. "Eight days inside" is counted from the 284th.
    49	- Cleon looks away from the boy on purpose and keeps that, and says no more than the leaf says. Karis does not theorize. The record's fear is reported, never endorsed.
    50	
    51	## What the author owns
    52	
    53	The chamber's light on the leaf, and the length of the silence before Karis reads. The texture of the meal. The route of the tail. How Lira reads the page. The pacing of the fire's voices within the fixed order: Lira first, then the circle, then Vastin, then Cael.
    54	
    55	## Where we leave pressure
    56	
    57	"Now what." There is a bearing, a set of marks nobody can read yet, and a site at the end of the line that has been quiet since they built the machine. He wants to stand in the middle of it. Tomorrow comes the list of parts, then the road east.
