editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:10:> **[Coordinator rulings after the Movement 1 audit, 2026-10-11 — binding; they override any plan text below that differs.]** (1) **Teague's spear is a tall MAN** (he / him): the locked Book 7 wrote him so (ch25, ch51, ch52), and Book 8 follows its own edition (OWNER-pending #59). Where the plan says "the tall woman", read "the tall man"; his silence toward the six until his question at the pass stands. (2) **Teague can read** (locked Book 7 ch25: he read a slip twice). Never write that he cannot; if he does not read a sheet it is because it is not in front of him or he has no need. (3) **Lira's asking:** she asked Oryn once about the ankle on the mountain in Book 7 and asked nobody for anything from then until Thornwater; do not call Thornwater her first ask since Norhold. (4) **The stroke and bar** is on stake thirty-two (the Stair's newer stake and the kit's unused one) and on the fourth site's thirty-four ONLY; stakes thirty-one and thirty-three do not carry it. Later records may show the grade on survey SHEETS; the field stakes do not all carry it. (5) **The cord:** the kit's cord is twenty strides, knotted at the fives (four knots to a length); Book 7's Ring was sixty-two cords and twenty strides round. The court is about 1,107 yards across, which is about FIFTY cords, not 159. Give no yardage for a cord. (6) **"West"** was first said aloud at the six-person table on the 268th (Karis's protected "It's west… Treswick…" speech, printed once in ch6). (7) **Deployment since the Line is twenty-nine** at the end of Movement 1 (two uses of the Iron read in earnest); trials are not counted.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:12:> **[Coordinator rulings after the Movement 2 audit, 2026-10-11 — binding; they override any plan text below that differs.]** (1) **Vastin's second paper is "the page": a COPY in his own hand** of one line from an old register ("—of the Architect: see the lower archive at Treswick, which holds it in full—"). It was never cut from anything and is never called a leaf; "the leaf" is the chamber record of Movement 6 only. (2) **The technician's sheet carries a Compact date (a registry year and a day in it) that is NEVER printed as figures** anywhere in this book; whoever reads it reads a date, and the page does not give its numbers. The office filed that sheet at the end of the second row of the records, and it lies there. (3) **The anomaly column:** on every survey abstract, in every hand, for six years, the entry is the one word *Total* — an entry, not a sum. (4) **The Fallow completion report** carries five strokes for a name and a count of six (locked Book 7), not five written names. (5) **What Vastin has told the six about the layer is four things only:** no key (it cannot be reached); the citation; the suppressed records; the technician's line. He has not defined "classification event" and does not know which event is meant. Nothing on the page says that menders, technicians or any office have tried to open it or know more. (6) **Speakers:** "What follows you," was Lira's; "She's right. Go and lie down, and don't take the stairs fast," was Oryn's. (7) **Deployment since the Line is thirty** at the end of Movement 2 (the Iron read at the landing on the 277th). Purse 118 marks. (8) **Teague's spear** has "he/his" on the page from chapter 7 (OWNER-pending #59 as defaulted). (9) Vastin has shown no Iron Wall, has no stated age, has asked only for a bed, and holds Karis's unsealed receipt. Cael has not touched the page and has not read the sheet's date closely.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:18:  - Reviewer-only fourth-site evidence: closed Book 7 edition `manuscript/chapter-58.md:117–229` and Book 7 STATE_LEDGER AFTER MOVEMENT 8. The author does not open it under O3. [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 26]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:25:It is dawn on the 299th, at Millrace ford. There are twelve and a mule. Teague's wrist is wrapped. Vastin is on day 20. Karis is writing with the bound hand. Oryn's road runs east with them for a day and a half and then it does not.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:29:The leg goes on the page as the place where two crews learn each other, and where the young one becomes someone a reader will grieve. Then the fourth site: a watch-post, a barricade, a captain's line, and a width that wins because the people inside the line have stood there before, with nothing gained by it. The thirteenth arrives. The next night every finding goes onto one blanket, the lamps finding is said aloud and filed on its own page, and a marshal finds a crack he does not pry.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:34:  - **The cairn at noon on the 300th:** Oryn looks once, straight, and walks on east.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:37:  - "Known" is entered under each date. The crest at dusk on the 303rd.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:38:- **The crest.** The watch-post: hut, fire, kit under a hide, two timbers, seven hoods, two crossbows, one low practitioner. "They knew." Seln: "That iron's been in the ground years. Not one cold term." [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: OWNER-pending #48] Teague: "Drawn?" Cael draws it. "Nobody declares. Nobody dies. They're seven people on a posting. Noted?" / Teague's **first "Noted."**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:42:  3. The watch reforms. **"Nothing was gained inside" is entered first.** "By count." Five go over stake thirty-four (Cael, then Lira, Karis, the young one, Vastin) and four stay on the shelf. They walk. The pinch. Eleven seconds. "You'll die in there." / "We've been in three times." The watch goes east one at a time and is not pursued.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:43:  4. The broad man goes over the sink's edge at the fourth second, and Teague does not turn.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:45:  **Win sentence, verbatim.** Oryn sets and knits the leg and is grey for a quarter-hour. The healers nod. Teague's arm: "That's a fact about a line." / "Noted" / "Everybody says that now." Brom's week of colours.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:46:- **The Span itself (noon).** An arch on two piers over the sink. Carvings on the piers' inner faces, copied. No steps: the arch is walked as a road rises. The bearing runs "Through". **Nothing happens on the crown.** The thirteenth listens and the ribs know the cost. **The log, verbatim.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:47:- **The shale camp (305th).** The blanket and its contents. The rows lean along the bearing. The point is fixed with a thumbnail circle.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:48:  - **The lamps finding, verbatim.** Vastin: "If a man designed the apparatus, then the sigils —" / the ruler rule. Two pages. Vastin's third "Noted." **Cael does not add his own third page.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:55:**Cutaways (~5,500):** Seln, ~1,800, on the crest at night or along the perimeter before dawn. He reads the iron and the watch. Seln's locked case stays shut and unopened. [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 26] Teague, ~1,700, in the watch's hut after the fall. He counts his crew; the broad man's leg; the young one asleep. **Nothing of the mechanism. Not the young one's name.** Karis, ~2,000, the night after the lamps finding. She holds the refusal in her own head, knows the six-word sentence exists, and does not write it.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:56:**Development:** about 15 Cael beats. Supporting: Teague 2, the young one 2, Karis 2, Vastin 2, Seln 1–2, Oryn 2, Brom 1, Lira 1.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:63:- The two pages stay separate in every head. Never use *terminal*, *circuit* or *infrastructure*. "Recent administration" means **the Compact**. Nobody reaches for "someone else".
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:64:- The cairn is on the 300th. Count Oryn's days from it (§12 C3). No cutaway at the court.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:69:The leg's country, camps and weather. How the seep is solved. The watch's behaviour in detail. The crown's view. The blanket's order of work. The humour of two men on sticks at one fire who never mention it.
