editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:19:  - From `BOOK_MAP.md`: §2 items 27–31; §3 A, C (294th; road east); §5 (the Teague cutaway); §7.1 (Force; Rune; the still place); §10 Tier A 11, 16, 23, 25, 27 and the S17–S18 Tier C lines; §12 C2, C4; §13 (the "Noted" order; Vastin's order).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:24:It is the 294th day. The list of parts takes all day, and Cleon's finger is on the last line at the bell. Twelve fragments. Karis's hand is bound and she writes with it anyway. Vastin is on day 15 of a month. There is still no mule.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:28:The book turns east, on the same road read backwards. Two crews join by contract and not by friendship. Cael watches the Force line in a meadow and does not yet know where it will matter. The grade is cracked, and the sites run oldest-last into the deep edge. At Millrace the healer reads him as deep as she goes. Meanwhile, and against the card, the second instrument turns inward by itself. We are in the last third now: progression surfaces at turning points, and the grade's vocabulary is counted separately (§7.2).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:31:- **The list of parts and the goodbye (294th).** "Your hand's better than mine on the fourth line." At the iron door: **"Work. Not a finding."** / **"Mind the stair. It leans."**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:32:- **The road east (295th–297th; ~5,000).** On the bridge he counts five piers, and does not look at the crown. The spring, with the wind in their faces this time. The fork passed. The shoulder hold's factor: "He said you'd say that." **The cut revisited:** "Here." Vastin puts his weight on the knee with the stick off the ground, once. "Two words. Both of them ours." / "Noted" (Cael's). The feeling of being *known* is entered under each date.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:33:- **Lowmarch (297th).** Pike: *Treswick. Survey read. Bearing.* The price and outcome columns are left blank, and the season line is dated. Cael reads the line the right way up. **Teague's term and contract, verbatim:** ten on a wall's count; shares by count; the field is Teague's; the reading is Karis's. "Contract. Not more than that." / "The wall's still the wall." Cael prices it honestly: Teague is the better field captain, and the rival clock still runs.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:35:- **The grade cracked (298th morning).** Teague is at the door for the dividers, not the marks. There are three marks; the box for the first tier is ruled and never used. Cleon's list puts the kindling mark and the sheet mark in one line: "A mark is a grade." Ages by first sheet: 61, 94, 138, 206. The third-tier point falls past the fourth, in the straightedge's shadow. **Oldest-last.** "It's observation … Not what it means." **Vastin's first "Noted."** Teague: "Oldest last." / "Then that's where we're going." **The log, verbatim** (the grandmother is *Cael's*: §12 C4).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:36:- **Millrace (298th evening).** "Eleven off the ridge." / "I know." The healers exchange one look, then both look at Brom's shoulder. Vastin is ordered to stand ("Nineteen days." / "Then it's eleven more."); it is his first order taken without walking it back. Oryn restates her terms: three holds owed, and "a stop on my own route". "Sixth chair." / "On my terms. Which are the only kind." **She asks each patient, "May I?"** The readings: Brom's shoulder; Lira's arm ("You listened when it told you the second time." / "Once." / "Once is once more than I priced"); Karis's hand ("Who sewed this."); the knee ("It held in a cut"; "Noted" / "That's new." / "It's a useful word." / "It's his.").
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:37:- **The deep reading (~3,000).** "May I?" / "Yes." It is the long one. Her current goes round the place. **The twelfth turns inward unbidden: *still*, then *set*.** It is not named, and he keeps the check out of his wrist and the change out of his face. The eyes pay in the dark. **Oryn's finding, verbatim.** He withholds his own and enters his reasons in order. Lira offers the leaf. "Is it a finding?" / "It's a leaf …" / "Then it's not mine … Tell me on the road, if there's road. Not at my table."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:38:- **Dawn (299th).** Twelve and a mule. The pencil line runs from the fourth circle onto the blank sheet and past the divider's point.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:40:**Physical challenge:** the road and the cut walked again on a bad knee. Force seen. As a learning encounter, the two crews work together in the Lowmarch meadow, **silent movement and march order only. They do not drill under a wall** (§13).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:42:**Development:** about 14 Cael beats. Supporting: Karis 2, Oryn 2, Vastin 2, Teague 2, Lira 1, Brom 1, the young one 1, Pike 1.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:46:- **Force is seen, not acquired.** The thirteenth comes at the Span's barricade.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:47:- The Rune finding is **told to no one**. Oryn's finding is hers, whole. The two instruments' disagreement stays unresolved.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:48:- Oryn does **not** hear the leaf. Cleon is not above ground; his goodbye is at the iron door.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:49:- The grade is observation only, with no who and no why. No first-tier site appears. "Four hundred years" occurs only in the fixed 298th log.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:50:- "Noted" order: Vastin's first is here. Teague does not say it yet.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:51:- The wall's count is the crew's six, Karis included, plus Teague's four. The healers are not on it.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:55:How the road east reads in reverse. The plank room's crowd. The meadow's details. Teague's crew at the table. How the grade's numbers come off the sheets. Millrace's lean-to, light and noise. How long the deep reading takes on the page.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:59:Twelve walk east along a straightedge's line, two of them on no wall's count. A healer's route and a researcher's archive ride on one mule. A boy carries two findings that do not agree and a warning that has started to lean. Five days out is a fence the Compact built, and somebody is still watching it.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:10:> **[Coordinator rulings after the Movement 1 audit, 2026-10-11 — binding; they override any plan text below that differs.]** (1) **Teague's spear is a tall MAN** (he / him): the locked Book 7 wrote him so (ch25, ch51, ch52), and Book 8 follows its own edition (OWNER-pending #59). Where the plan says "the tall woman", read "the tall man"; his silence toward the six until his question at the pass stands. (2) **Teague can read** (locked Book 7 ch25: he read a slip twice). Never write that he cannot; if he does not read a sheet it is because it is not in front of him or he has no need. (3) **Lira's asking:** she asked Oryn once about the ankle on the mountain in Book 7 and asked nobody for anything from then until Thornwater; do not call Thornwater her first ask since Norhold. (4) **The stroke and bar** is on stake thirty-two (the Stair's newer stake and the kit's unused one) and on the fourth site's thirty-four ONLY; stakes thirty-one and thirty-three do not carry it. Later records may show the grade on survey SHEETS; the field stakes do not all carry it. (5) **The cord:** the kit's cord is twenty strides, knotted at the fives (four knots to a length); Book 7's Ring was sixty-two cords and twenty strides round. The court is about 1,107 yards across, which is about FIFTY cords, not 159. Give no yardage for a cord. (6) **"West"** was first said aloud at the six-person table on the 268th (Karis's protected "It's west… Treswick…" speech, printed once in ch6). (7) **Deployment since the Line is twenty-nine** at the end of Movement 1 (two uses of the Iron read in earnest); trials are not counted.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:12:> **[Coordinator rulings after the Movement 2 audit, 2026-10-11 — binding; they override any plan text below that differs.]** (1) **Vastin's second paper is "the page": a COPY in his own hand** of one line from an old register ("—of the Architect: see the lower archive at Treswick, which holds it in full—"). It was never cut from anything and is never called a leaf; "the leaf" is the chamber record of Movement 6 only. (2) **The technician's sheet carries a Compact date (a registry year and a day in it) that is NEVER printed as figures** anywhere in this book; whoever reads it reads a date, and the page does not give its numbers. The office filed that sheet at the end of the second row of the records, and it lies there. (3) **The anomaly column:** on every survey abstract, in every hand, for six years, the entry is the one word *Total* — an entry, not a sum. (4) **The Fallow completion report** carries five strokes for a name and a count of six (locked Book 7), not five written names. (5) **What Vastin has told the six about the layer is four things only:** no key (it cannot be reached); the citation; the suppressed records; the technician's line. He has not defined "classification event" and does not know which event is meant. Nothing on the page says that menders, technicians or any office have tried to open it or know more. (6) **Speakers:** "What follows you," was Lira's; "She's right. Go and lie down, and don't take the stairs fast," was Oryn's. (7) **Deployment since the Line is thirty** at the end of Movement 2 (the Iron read at the landing on the 277th). Purse 118 marks. (8) **Teague's spear** has "he/his" on the page from chapter 7 (OWNER-pending #59 as defaulted). (9) Vastin has shown no Iron Wall, has no stated age, has asked only for a bed, and holds Karis's unsealed receipt. Cael has not touched the page and has not read the sheet's date closely.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:31:- **The Deepstacks (284th).** The galleries, the shelving, the smell of a place where nothing has been decided. Cleon reads to the end of his page first. The sheets are laid out 11/29/12. Karis: "Older than [UNBOUND]." Cleon: "I know that hand." "Being believed … It's the end of being able to be wrong." "Give me a week." Cael finds himself, for the first time, unfiled.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:32:- **The yard door (285th).** Vastin's reflex: "Vastin. Archmarshal, Compact enforcement. You'll find the name is —". **Seln answers truthfully** (ruling 25): "He's on the count … the form asks what a hand's for, not what he was." The narration records that Seln did not lie and what not lying cost him. "I'm sorry." / "Don't be sorry. Be nobody." Cael's fellow-feeling on the landing. **The log, verbatim.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:33:- **The chamber days (285th–289th; ~8,000 on the page, including the 288th–289th the source left undramatized).**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:35:  - Cleon's board against the Hall's fourth sheet: bearer, carried, ornament. "They're orders." **The limit, verbatim.** "Same make."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:38:  - **Vastin learning to be nobody**, badly. He moves toward the lamp four times on the fourth day. "How long did it take you." / "I was fourteen. I'm nineteen. I'm not there yet either."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:42:- **The alley (290th dusk; ~4,000, developed).** Staging follows BOOK_MAP §8. Vastin turns uphill and roots the cut wall to wall: "there is no round." Nobody declares. Brom with a loose step-stone. Lira's drop, the knife into the stave's shaft. Cael stands still at the plane's foot for a minute and some, as "the reason". Seln's weighted cord from the roof takes the signaller. The cache was on the roof the whole time. They leave: none taken, no faces, nobody dead.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:43:- **Costs and the acquisition.** Karis's left hand is cut on a step's edge. Brom binds it with thread, a strip of shirt and his teeth, because no healer inside the gate would put hands on it. Vastin is spent past the road and the knee goes again. **The Iron-Wall notice renders, verbatim.** "I put the wall in front of it anyway. I'd like that entered" / "It's entered." **Not told.** The faction's limit is entered as a finding. **The log, verbatim.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:47:**Development:** about 15 Cael beats. Supporting: Vastin 3, Brom 2, Seln 2, Karis 2, Cleon 2, Lira 1.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:52:- The eleventh is acquired in the alley's quiet middle minute, after Iron Wall has been witnessed in use: the cut first, then this full minute. It is **not deployed and not told** to Vastin.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:55:- No healer works inside the gate. Oryn is north.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:56:- Vastin does not know the mechanism and his age is not stated. "Forty years" is his rounding.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:8:- Owner names: no new names. The hood in the tail stays faceless. The hold child in Oryn's cutaway stays unnamed.
