editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-009.md:19:  - From `BOOK_MAP.md`: §1 Ending; §2 items 36–40; §3 A (the pass), C (burial; pacing); §5 (the Seln, Oryn and Vastin cutaways); §7.1 (the Force first use; Rune inward; the still place; the instruments; the Arbiter); §8 (the pass); §9; §10 Tier A 19–22 and the S21–S24 Tier C lines, including the closing prose; **§11**; §12 C3, C11; §13; §15.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-009.md:24:It is first light on the 306th, at the shale camp below the notch. Seln comes back wet to the ankle from the pass's floor. Twelve and a mule. Vastin is on day 27. The ribs have been quiet since the marsh, and the thirteenth is listening.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-009.md:36:  - The broad man is hit at the slant's high edge. **The young one goes out a stride to drag him and is killed by the sixth volley.** Oryn's hands are on him, and come off with nothing done. Vastin cannot move. The broad man says the name, once. [OWNER-pending #54]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-009.md:39:  - Vastin goes down. Karis sits with her bound hand on his shoulder. Teague kneels by his own dead. **"A wall keeps everyone behind it, and one of mine wasn't."** At the far mouth Cael understands that the line was not drawn in ink.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-009.md:40:- **Burial and the plain's edge (306th).** Teague's crew builds the cairn in their own order. The six carry at his leave. Lira and Seln recover the mule by the ridge path. **Eleven.** Oryn: "Ribs. May I?" / "Yes." **"That's a line. That's not yours." / "It's mine now."** No term tonight.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-009.md:41:- **The still place, read as made (~3,000).** He recalls the warning by heart. Then **the twelfth turned inward on purpose**: still; set; *bones*; *a floor with nothing built on it*; *an instruction with no language*. "The same kind of thing, to that instrument, as the sites were to Cleon's." He tells no one, not Lira, not Oryn, not Karis. The Arbiter is unchanged. **The instruments read wronger**: the cord a stride short, the edges a hair and a half to two out. The trend is up and he draws no line. **The log, verbatim** ("the whole year"). [OWNER-pending #58]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-009.md:43:- **At the line (dusk).** Every sigil goes dark at the same stride. Lira: "Right." Brom prices the stump. Karis: "It's the first one." Seln gives the count. Vastin: "This is where they drew it." Oryn steps in one stride and back: "Nothing. Everything, round it. Same as you." It goes unanswered. Teague steps in one stride and back: "Field's mine. This isn't field." The turning begins. **The fixed exchange, then "Wait here."**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-009.md:44:- **The centre.** 506 strides. At a hundred strides, the twelfth is turned on the floor: the same reading. The eyes pay. **No edge. No seam.** "Not the Quiet." "Not a fragment." "The same kind of made." He fit. It was not an accident. **The third sentence stays unsaid.** He counts the strides back.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-009.md:45:- **The line again.** Oryn: "May I?" / "Yes." "The same finding." Lira: "Well?" / "I'll tell you on the road. If there's road." He tells nobody what the centre felt like and gives them the count instead. "Twenty-nine tomorrow." / "Thirty's the month."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-009.md:46:- **The ledger, the letter and the dawn (307th night–308th), verbatim.** Teague: "After the next thaw … My crew comes." [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: OWNER-pending #48] Oryn: "The day I have to." … "After the thaw: bring the map, and lie still when I say." [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: OWNER-pending #48] "Six. Six and no mule." Vastin is unadmitted. "West." **Closing prose, verbatim.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-009.md:49:**Cutaways (~5,800):** Seln, ~1,800, on the ridge with Lira to recover the mule: the swept scree below, the dead pine. Oryn, ~2,000, the night after the first death under her hands. **She has not heard the leaf. No cutaway at the court.** Vastin, ~2,000, at the court's rim at night: the line he never asked about. **He is unadmitted and not asking. There is no hint of Book 9's request.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-009.md:50:**Development:** about 15 Cael beats. Supporting: Teague 2, Oryn 2, Lira 2, Vastin 2, Karis 1–2, Seln 1–2, Brom 1.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-009.md:58:- The death is brief and not graphic. Its cost carries: eleven, the gap where a fourth stood, and Teague one short and not saying the number. Nobody strikes a retreating opponent.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-009.md:59:- Vastin does not ask and is not asked; there is no vote. Oryn has not heard the leaf. Cael is nineteen.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-009.md:60:- Count Oryn's days past her road from the cairn (§12 C3). The letter's "Tell Lira's family I said so" stays verbatim (§12 C11). [OWNER-pending #55]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-009.md:68:West, six and no mule. Three holds still owe a healer a visit. A captain walks home past a cairn. A marshal with a stick has stood at the line where they drew it and has not asked. Thirteen fragments. A still place read by two instruments and understood by neither. A third sentence waits past *exclude* and *prevent* that he is not ready to write. Book 9 begins with that sentence.

