## 4. Standing defaults, names and Teague's spear

- **PASS — season-blind / measures / age / Path syntax.** A full scan of chapters 7–12 finds no named season or month, no English weekday, no metric unit, no numbered span since Cael's Kindling, no birthday, and no authorial “his Path” or “my Path” (`manuscript/chapter-07.md:1–287`; `chapter-08.md:1–267`; `chapter-09.md:1–277`; `chapter-10.md:1–283`; `chapter-11.md:1–259`; `chapter-12.md:1–299`). Generic *cold term*, *season* and *month* are permitted under OWNER #35/#42/#48 (`OWNER-DECISIONS.md:55–59,121–126,146–153`). Cael is called a boy of nineteen, matching the ledger (`manuscript/chapter-11.md:173–175`; `AUTHOR-REPORT.md:167`). Feet, yards, paces, strides and cords are used consistently (`manuscript/chapter-07.md:9,137–147`; `manuscript/chapter-09.md:61–89`; `manuscript/chapter-11.md:223–227`).
- **PASS — Reader Standard.** The flood danger, dead toes, Lira's fall and Vastin's collapse are concrete without gore or adult-only framing (`manuscript/chapter-07.md:153–167`; `manuscript/chapter-08.md:89–111`; `manuscript/chapter-09.md:45–57`; `manuscript/chapter-12.md:179–187`).
- **Teague's spear / tall man — PASS.** Every reference is male: “The tall man … he … his knees” (`manuscript/chapter-07.md:213–215`); “the tall man … his spear … his knees” (`manuscript/chapter-08.md:7`); “his pale eyes” (`:37`); “the tall man … he … but the tall man” (`:87`); “the tall man … his spear's butt” (`:127`); and “The tall man … he … his big chapped hands … he” (`manuscript/chapter-09.md:91`). No feminine or neutral pronoun is used for him. Teague separately reads the plank and Vastin's hands, consistent with the locked ruling that Teague can read (`manuscript/chapter-09.md:215,255`; `packets/MOVEMENT-002.md:10–11`).
- **Names — PASS.** No named person, place or animal is minted. Cael, Lira, Brom, Karis, Seln, Oryn, Pike, Teague, Ephram, Rooke, Vastin, Lowmarch, Thornwater, Ostrand, Treswick and the Path/faction terms all pre-exist the plan or closed text (`manuscript/chapter-06.md:221–295`; `packets/MOVEMENT-002.md:14–73`). “The Architect” is a protected title, explicitly not a name (`manuscript/chapter-12.md:65–79`; `BOOK_MAP.md:335`). The ferryman, broker, three road strangers, Teague's crew and Oryn's patients remain unnamed (`manuscript/chapter-07.md:135–167,213–243`; `manuscript/chapter-08.md:205–255`).

