# Plan audit — Movement 6 (chapters 38–44)

## Verdict

**REPAIR — fourteen line fixes in chapters 38–44, followed by owner/coordinator resolution of two protected-text/calendar conflicts.** The telling, birthday, integration, five findings, shooting arc, mule transfer, debt, deployment count, bodies, money, and withheld truths otherwise ratify. The two unresolved conflicts are protected *Tomorrow makes three* at dawn on day 111 versus the next actual Quieting entry on day 114 (`manuscript/chapter-44.md:215–217`; `packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:26–33`), and the restored protected promise that Oryn will be “three days north” when the crew is back at the board versus Lowmarch on day 112 and Oryn at Millrace, south of Lowmarch, on day 113 (`source chapter-16.md:127`; `STATE_LEDGER.md:38–40,55`; `packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:20,26,30`). Neither may be repaired by altering protected wording.

## 1. Continuity with the closed text

The movement’s carried state agrees with the Movement 5 close. Deployment enters and leaves at thirteen (`manuscript/chapter-33.md:221–223`; `manuscript/chapter-39.md:245`; `manuscript/chapter-40.md:385`); Shadow remains the single sealed Ring use and is not used here (`manuscript/chapter-33.md:201`; `manuscript/chapter-39.md:61–79`; `AUTHOR-REPORT.md:12`). Cael enters with nine fragments and acquires Tide-adjacent as the tenth on day 100, then uses it only for listening and one self-reading (`manuscript/chapter-37.md:279–305`; `manuscript/chapter-38.md:37–49`; `manuscript/chapter-40.md:319–373`). The two day-96 private tests remain tests, not deployments (`STATE_LEDGER.md:442`; `manuscript/chapter-44.md:11–27`).

Bodies carry correctly. Movement 5 closes Lira’s left forearm mended but under the no-use order, right ankle unmended, Karis voiceless, Brom’s four string cuts open, and Cael’s calf/forearm hurt (`manuscript/chapter-33.md:193–195`). Movement 6 keeps Lira’s left arm slung and unused, releases only the right tibia on day 110, and leaves the ankle taped (`manuscript/chapter-42.md:103–121`; `manuscript/chapter-43.md:125–153`); Brom’s hand is sound and the hook is on his belt (`manuscript/chapter-41.md:73–79`; `manuscript/chapter-43.md:153–155`); Karis’s voice returns but is barred from lecturing for a week (`manuscript/chapter-43.md:153–155`); Cael’s calf is a closed seam and his forearm only yellow-marked (`manuscript/chapter-38.md:231–249`; `manuscript/chapter-43.md:157–159`). Oryn’s mule remains with the crew under OWNER #24 (`manuscript/chapter-43.md:171–215`; `manuscript/chapter-44.md:213–225`).

Objects and accounts also carry. The three boxes, Seln’s shut case, Hesk’s satchel and papers, eleven rubbings, calfskin, crossbow, hook and five bolts remain accounted for (`manuscript/chapter-41.md:3–21`; `manuscript/chapter-42.md:205–277`; `manuscript/chapter-43.md:171–215`; `manuscript/chapter-44.md:145–219`). Cash begins at 108, pays six to Thornwater, and closes at 102 (`STATE_LEDGER.md:607`; `manuscript/chapter-40.md:55–67,379`). Pike’s Fallow wording arrives on bark, while Gault’s line is only Cael’s memory; no physical Gault leaf appears (`manuscript/chapter-40.md:221–251`). Seven hounds remain unaccounted for (`STATE_LEDGER.md:591`; `AUTHOR-REPORT.md:179`).

Knowledge boundaries hold. Oryn receives the mechanism and sources by Path, with only Lira, Brom and Karis identifiable from her own touch (`manuscript/chapter-38.md:19–35`); Seln is called Shadow once in the barn while Oryn is outside, and her later hand on his shoulder is not read (`manuscript/chapter-41.md:65–91`; `manuscript/chapter-42.md:3–11`; `manuscript/chapter-44.md:113–117`). The six know Cael’s day-96 test and that his self-reading found *something*, but only Cael knows its content (`manuscript/chapter-44.md:11–27,167–209`). Karis’s hypothesis remains hers and unstated (`manuscript/chapter-43.md:59–107`; `manuscript/chapter-44.md:59–69`).

No closed-text contradiction survives apart from the two protected/calendar conflicts in the verdict. Fixes 6–12 below address plan-level reserved-agency violations, not changes to the event canon.

## 2. The movement plan and owner flags

All packet beats occur in order: telling and cost (`ch38:3–179`), listening and yard practice (`ch38:281–305`; `ch39:55–291`), birthday/Pike/self-reading (`ch40:3–385`), tables and the Quieting (`ch41:3–303`), findings two and three plus the bow (`ch42:3–337`), findings four and five, mule decision and Lira-first telling (`ch43:3–349`), then the circle, Vastin, rule, debt and Oryn window (`ch44:3–301`). The withheld items hold: no outward Tide reading, no debt payment, no stated Karis hypothesis, one aloud `[UNBOUND]`, no source identification of Seln to Oryn, and the anomaly remains “something”/“a place” rather than receiving the still-place phrase (`ch40:343–373`; `ch42:269`; `ch43:59–107`; `ch44:167–209`).

Owner flags rule as follows.

1. **Karis’s rank — KEEP manuscript; AMEND packet.** “An Ember. Iron, third rank” and three represented tiers agree with the retained Iron Rank Three ledger state (`manuscript/chapter-42.md:7–11`; `BOOK_MAP.md:21`). The packet’s “no ranking” entry is the error (`packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:45`).
2. **The still place — KEEP this movement’s avoidance; AMEND the M7/M8 coordination.** Locked Books 5–6 already call the anomaly “the still place from session nine” or “the still place I don’t count” (`book-05 manuscript/chapter-01.md:121`; `chapter-45.md:31`; `chapter-60.md:25`; `book-06 manuscript/chapter-34.md:229`). Avoiding the phrase through M7 remains workable because Cael owes the finding to Oryn and has not made it shared speech (`manuscript/chapter-44.md:167–209`). M8’s novelty is location and disclosure, not coinage (`packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:22,29`). Binding note proposed for M7 and M8: **“[Coordinator note — still-place continuity, binding.] ‘The still place’ is an established private log label in locked Books 5–6, not a new phrase in Movement 8. Movement 7 must not spend the new beat: keep Cael’s finding private, unnamed aloud, and owed to Oryn. In Movement 8, the beat is that the old log label becomes a repeatedly read LOCATION and a shared spoken finding: after the second and third self-readings, Cael attaches ‘the still place’ to the located anomaly, tells Oryn while reading her with permission, and she answers the finding. Do not present the words as newly coined or new to the reader; preserve ‘Not the Quiet. Not a fragment.’ and all withheld-source limits.”** The protected standing words are properly retired here because the anomaly has changed from unseen/unlocatable to locatable and repeatable; observation replaces patience (`manuscript/chapter-40.md:353–373`; `BOOK_MAP.md:285`).
3. **“Tomorrow makes three” — OWNER.** Written as day 111 breaks, “tomorrow” is day 112, when the crew goes to Lowmarch; the Stair is entered on day 114 (`manuscript/chapter-44.md:215–223`; `STATE_LEDGER.md:38–41`; `packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:26–33`). There is only one prior Quieting entry, the Ring on day 96. No honest gloss makes three. Preserve the protected line until the owner either releases its placement to the night of day 113 (unchanged words, immediately before the Stair) or supplies protected replacement wording (`BOOK_MAP.md:287`).
4. **Practice/deployment — KEEP.** Eleven small Wind leans are explicitly fenced as practice, as the two private day-96 tests were; the Ring’s Anchor perception counted because it was a deliberate operational release in the fight (`manuscript/chapter-39.md:167–245`; `STATE_LEDGER.md:442`; `manuscript/chapter-33.md:219–223`). Thirteen is correct.
5. **Oryn’s answer — KEEP withheld from Cael and reader.** Her refusal denies retrospective consent and denies confession-as-payment (`manuscript/chapter-38.md:145–155,225–229`).
6. **Five further days — KEEP.** The eighth bite mark is slow on day 106; Oryn remains through the day-110 fortnight check, converting intended departure day 106 to actual day 111 (`manuscript/chapter-41.md:99`; `manuscript/chapter-42.md:103–121`; `manuscript/chapter-43.md:125–167`).
7. **North/Millrace — OWNER after protected restoration.** The northern wicket and later west/south bend are locally plausible (`manuscript/chapter-44.md:213–223,295–301`), but the full protected unit says she will be three days north when the crew returns to the board (`source chapter-16.md:127`). The crew is back at Lowmarch day 112 and Oryn is at Millrace, one day south of Lowmarch, day 113 (`STATE_LEDGER.md:38–40,55`; `packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:26,30`). A road bend cannot reconcile those assertions.
8. **Seln’s Path — KEEP.** It is spoken once with Oryn absent and never inferred from her unread touch (`manuscript/chapter-41.md:65–91`; `manuscript/chapter-42.md:3–11`; `manuscript/chapter-44.md:113–117`).
9. **Lira’s “thirty-two” — KEEP.** It is explicitly a guess about a numeral, answered by Karis’s ignorance, not a decoded index (`manuscript/chapter-43.md:3–21`; `BOOK_MAP.md:337`).
10. **Apple language — KEEP.** “A month before,” “a fortnight after,” and “before the snow’s a week old” name neither a month nor a season, do not count back to a birthday, and fit the established frost/cold-road weather before snow (`manuscript/chapter-40.md:75–111,275–289`; `STATE_LEDGER.md:487,573`).
11. **“The last time” — KEEP.** It supplies no interval to the former birthday (`manuscript/chapter-40.md:185–193,311`).
12. **Founding stone — KEEP, with reserved-agency repairs 11–12.** The old gate footing and civic dating custom contradict no bible, map or later packet and give no numerical year (`manuscript/chapter-42.md:205–217`; `BOOK_MAP.md:333–334`).
13. **Length — KEEP.** The 37,523-word movement is about four percent over the target, with the five findings and required windows present (`AUTHOR-REPORT.md:7,16–24,37–41`). This is not a canon or plan failure.
14. **Reader grade — KEEP.** The first scene states harm, touch, conditions and cost in direct concrete language and withholds forgiveness; the reported grade is 3.44 (`manuscript/chapter-38.md:105–179,203–249`; `AUTHOR-REPORT.md:11`).

The telling passes the packet’s strict standard. Oryn names the wrong as turning her own table around, states that the taking did not empty her hands but did run beside her and then in him, tests five patients, sets a price Cael cannot prepay, orders self first/tell her/ask first, and withholds her answer (`manuscript/chapter-38.md:105–179,203–267`; `manuscript/chapter-39.md:265–287`). Cael does not argue his reasons, win consent after the fact, or receive pardon (`manuscript/chapter-38.md:125–155,225–229`). The Book 6 retelling is true in meaning: Arbiter wake at Kindling, eleven dark seconds, failed-safe word in place of the older name, then darkness (`book-06 manuscript/chapter-36.md:117–121`; `chapter-37.md:13–17`; `chapter-39.md:59–63,117–121`; `book-07 manuscript/chapter-38.md:5–9`).

## 3. Calendar

The ordinary day chain is exact:

- day 100: telling and first listening (`ch38:79,189`; `ch39:55`);
- day 101: grain, Storm and Wind practice (`ch39:119–245`);
- day 102: birthday, cash and first self-reading (`ch40:3,55–67,189–211,319–379`);
- days 103–105: flat Ring, count, word and first finding (`ch41:3,65,125,165,209`);
- days 106–108: second and third findings and bow lessons (`ch42:3,129,175,205,283`);
- days 108–110: fourth/fifth findings, arm check and gate-walk (`ch43:3,59,125,291–349`);
- day 110 night to day 111 dawn: six-person council, rule and departure (`ch44:3–13,135,145–223`);
- days 111–112: Oryn’s window (`ch44:223–301`).

The birthday is day 102 and “Nineteen” sits at the mapped meal point without forbidden calendar adjacency (`manuscript/chapter-40.md:189–211`; `BOOK_MAP.md:31,284`). Oryn’s arithmetic is sound: nine late on day 104, eleven late at the intended day-106 departure, sixteen out on day 111, and seventeen at Oxhollow on day 121 (`manuscript/chapter-41.md:99`; `manuscript/chapter-43.md:125–167`; `manuscript/chapter-44.md:245–249`). The only calendar failures are protected *Tomorrow makes three* and protected “three days north,” ruled in §2 flags 3 and 7.

## 4. Standing defaults

Pass. Chapters 38–44 contain no named season, named month, month order, English weekday, metric unit, year count since Kindling, or “his Path” for Cael; “Third-day” is the academy term and “month”/“fortnight” are durations (`manuscript/chapter-42.md:315–317`; `manuscript/chapter-43.md:149,335`). Cael is nineteen only from day 102 onward (`manuscript/chapter-40.md:189–211`). Feet, yards, paces, strides, hands and cords are permitted local/imperial measures (`manuscript/chapter-41.md:7–21`; `manuscript/chapter-44.md:239`). The prose remains Reader Standard; the consent-and-cost scene is especially explicit without becoming abstract (`manuscript/chapter-38.md:105–179`).

## 5. Protected text

All mapped and packet-quoted protected units other than the three markers are present once and verbatim. This includes the table and yard conditions (`ch38:159–175`; `ch39:283–287`), Karis’s instrument line (`ch39:45`), birthday/Pike/log units (`ch40:211–251,373–383`), all Quieting entries including the struck six and sole `[UNBOUND]` (`ch41:195`; `ch42:27–65,269–277`; `ch43:69–107`), the gate-walk exchange (`ch43:319–327`), the circle/Vastin units (`ch44:51–139`), and the rule and second pole (`ch44:155,179,197,217`). No protected document is printed twice after fix 13 removes the composed “morning/seventeen at Oxhollow” anticipation (`manuscript/chapter-43.md:161`; `source chapter-16.md:127`).

The three full-source restorations are:

- **ch38:181 — Oryn to Cael.** Full unit is source `chapter-14.md:47`. It requires Cael standing, Oryn handing him Hesk’s book, and Cael lying down again; fixes 1–3 repair both joins.
- **ch39:275 — Cael to Oryn.** Full unit is source `chapter-14.md:97`. Its own breastbone gesture replaces the manuscript’s anticipatory hand gesture; fixes 4–5 prevent repetition.
- **ch44:105 — Oryn to the assembled five, with the last sentence directed to Cael.** Full unit is source `chapter-16.md:127`. Fix 14 restores it immediately before the already-protected “Don’t go in without me” unit (`manuscript/chapter-44.md:107–109`). Fix 13 removes prose that had independently composed the protected unit’s “morning” and “seventeen at Oxhollow” content (`manuscript/chapter-43.md:161`).

The mandatory edition bans require no changes inside any of those units: none contains a named season/month, metric unit, year-since-Kindling count, or obsolete edition name. The source wording is therefore restored without alteration.

## 6. New canon minted

**KEEP:** Oryn’s cost and felt experience (`ch38:105–149,203–249`); Tide listening, Storm resettling, Wind correction and first self-reading (`ch38:281–305`; `ch39:55–245`; `ch40:319–373`); Brom’s forge/house recollection (`ch39:93–115`); Thornwater husband, boy, apples and grain economy (`ch39:119–127`; `ch40:75–137`); the hold’s yard crossbow and Lira’s one-armed arc (`ch41:73–79`; `ch42:129–201,283–337`; `ch43:229–281`); Brom’s hook and five bolts (`ch41:73–79`; `ch43:153–155`); word to Pike (`ch40:221–251`); the Quieting grammar and three-leaf restraint (`ch41:165–283`); finding four, the amendment, Lira’s recovery, Oryn’s lateness, mule transfer, four wheres, debt terms and physical road bend (`ch43:3–215`; `ch44:71–95,167–209,223–301`). None conflicts with the bible, map or M7 packet. The husband, boy, bowman and patients remain unnamed as required (`packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:8`; `manuscript/chapter-40.md:75–137`; `chapter-42.md:129–201`).

**KEEP specifically:** the “founding stone” from Ostrand’s old gate, the hold’s yard crossbow, the unnamed husband, and the unnamed hold boy (`manuscript/chapter-42.md:129–151,205–217`; `manuscript/chapter-40.md:75–137`). They add local material culture without displacing any later beat or owner-held name.

**AMEND:** the flat-Ring analysis currently invents a cutter, tired arm and mason behind the unidentified marks (`manuscript/chapter-41.md:37,55,133,151,153`), beyond the map’s exhaustive allowance for indefinite agency (`BOOK_MAP.md:333`). Fixes 6–10 return it to observable variation. Finding three likewise assigns intention and a single hand to the band (`manuscript/chapter-42.md:221,255`); fixes 11–12 retain the physical evidence but remove the forbidden maker inference. **CUT:** none; every minted event survives after those sentence-level amendments.

Oryn’s road bend is KEEP as terrain, but it cannot validate the restored protected “three days north”; that remains the owner conflict in §2.7 (`manuscript/chapter-44.md:295–301`; `source chapter-16.md:127`).

## 7. Names

Pass. Every proper name in chapters 38–44 is already in the map, ledger or packet: Cael, Lira, Brom, Karis, Seln, Oryn, Hesk, Pike, Gault, Vastin, Daeva, Reydan, Denvash, Ardenmere, Ostrand, Oxhollow, Thornwater, Fallow, Fenmark and Ternhall (`BOOK_MAP.md:17–22,257–269`; `STATE_LEDGER.md:210–228`). No animal is named. The husband, boy, bowman, carters, patients, old woman and mule remain unnamed (`manuscript/chapter-40.md:75–137`; `chapter-42.md:129–201`; `chapter-44.md:223–301`).

## 8. Next-movement inheritance

Movement 7’s packet already carries the day-111 start, Oryn gone, mule with the crew, Lira two weeks into the order, and the report west (`packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:20`). It must additionally inherit:

- **Cael:** nineteen; ten fragments; deployment thirteen; Shadow still only once; the eleven Wind leans are practice; the tenth has read only himself, once; two further self-readings on different days and the whole telling to Oryn remain owed; he may read nobody merely to test the ability; Oryn’s answer and remaining price stay withheld (`manuscript/chapter-39.md:245`; `chapter-40.md:189–211,319–385`; `chapter-44.md:167–209`).
- **Bodies:** Lira’s left arm remains slung and may hold nothing until first snow, although all eight marks have taken; right tibia may run; right ankle remains taped/unmended and her left arm cannot span the bow. Brom’s hand is whole. Karis’s voice is whole but she must not lecture for a week. Cael’s calf is closed and forearm yellow-marked. Seln is unhurt (`manuscript/chapter-42.md:103–121,129–201`; `chapter-43.md:125–159`).
- **Equipment and money:** 102 marks in hand; three boxes and Oryn’s mule; Seln’s shut case; Oryn’s empty pannier left on the saddle while she carries the other and the spare rope; the yard crossbow, belt hook and five bolts travel with Brom; the ring sheets, bark slips, four chips, calfskin rings and charcoal round remain in Karis’s boxes (`manuscript/chapter-40.md:55–67,379`; `chapter-41.md:3–39`; `chapter-42.md:205–277`; `chapter-43.md:171–215`; `chapter-44.md:209–245`).
- **Knowledge:** all six know Cael functioned inside the Ring and know that his self-reading found something, but none except Cael knows what; Oryn knows the mechanism but not that Seln supplied Shadow; Karis’s hypothesis is neither spoken nor entered; the Quieting name and five findings are shared; nobody has put a verb between the facts (`manuscript/chapter-44.md:11–105,113–117`).
- **Research state:** Karis’s kinds-count is covered and unsaid; finding four says only “five or six”; stake thirty-two remains Lira’s guess; the four wheres include two map rings marked *guess* and Seln’s unplaced childhood round (`manuscript/chapter-41.md:125–159`; `chapter-43.md:3–53`; `chapter-44.md:71–95`).
- **Open accounts:** Pike has eight completed lines but the crew has not heard the eighth read at the board; the Fallow hundred remains in Pike’s box, the ferryman’s rope and two HOLD slips remain unresolved, Hesk’s parcel has not arrived, three letters are unanswered, and seven hounds remain untracked (`manuscript/chapter-40.md:221–263,383`; `AUTHOR-REPORT.md:173–179`).
- **Oryn:** day 112 closes just short of the mill; she is sixteen late out of Thornwater and seventeen late at Oxhollow, has left the mule, and has not forgiven Cael or received the self-reading (`manuscript/chapter-44.md:223–301`). Her exact location on day 113 is Millrace under M7, subject to the protected north conflict (`packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:30`).

