editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-17.md:205:He counted them. It was not hard. He lifted each sheet by its lower corner with one finger, and let it fall upon the last, and said the number in his head; the stock was soft, and it clung a little, and twice he went back three sheets to be sure that he had not lifted two together. He came to the row's foot, and to a figure.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-18.md:53:He looked at that squarely, standing over a spring on a moor with a sheet in his sleeve.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-18.md:79:He crossed the turf, and made no more noise than he ever did. He set the sheet down between those two hands, with its head away from the boy, as every paper had lain before him in his life. He squared it with one finger. Then he went back to the water, and stood with his face to the mule. He counted the sound of the spring, since a man who has placed a thing does not watch it found.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-13.md:231:"May I ask a thing that I ought perhaps to have asked this morning?" Vastin had his bread in his hand, and he did not lower himself onto a stone until he had the question out. "You have told me what I am to do if one of them comes at me. You have not told me what I am to do if it comes at one of you."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-14.md:243:They came over the north bank at the mark, as Lira had said that they would, and he turned his head as far as a post may. There were five, grey and long, pouring over the worn places with their heads level. And behind those, out from under the strip that nobody had been able to see, there came three more.
