editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:31:- **The reading inward (281st, the six-mile post).** First he works out the line between "stop touching it" and "do not read yourself". Then come the fourth and fifth readings. The ten are named as currents. The still place is read *around*, not touched. **Finding: the reading feels current; the still place has none; "a cord on a stone."** He needs an instrument for what does not move. He writes down later that he is afraid of that.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:46:- No fragment is acquired here. The still place is not touched or turned on, and the twelfth does not yet exist.
