editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:31:- **The Deepstacks (284th).** The galleries, the shelving, the smell of a place where nothing has been decided. Cleon reads to the end of his page first. The sheets are laid out 11/29/12. Karis: "Older than [UNBOUND]." Cleon: "I know that hand." "Being believed … It's the end of being able to be wrong." "Give me a week." Cael finds himself, for the first time, unfiled.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-001.md:26:Put the cold term on the page [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 19] and teach hard. This is the first third, so the formula wants progression vocabulary at its densest here. The reader should finish the movement knowing all ten fragments as costs and limits, and the kit as a tool. They should know that instruments read wrong in one pair of hands, and why Karis cannot let go of the index. The movement ends with six at a table and a word nobody has said yet: west.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-002.md:55:  Vastin is sent to bed ("don't take the stairs fast"). Cael's hand stays a hand's width from the page. Nobody says *west*.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-002.md:77:A page lies on the bare end of a table with a title and a place written on it. The place is west, inside walls. Cael's hand has been near it for the length of a lamp and has not touched it. A thing that is not yet his is a thing he can still refuse, and everyone in the room knows he won't.
