24:- **Objects/accounts:** the tarred-canvas kit case, strap, cord knotted at the fives, unused stake 32 with stroke/bar and bright turned point, and mallet are at the back-room table; the dead man's ledger is shut beside them. Three boxes stand at the warm wall. The cart-and-gelding reserve remains sealed under five thumbprints in the third box, separate from the 96-mark living purse. The Fallow hundred and Stair 300 remain in Pike's box, unmarked and not crew-payable debts. The ferryman is owed 60 yards of four-strand rope, not wanted before the thaw. The forty-mark axe-head fence is taken and not begun. Teague forfeited the four-mark weir slip. The six-mark back room is paid through the cold term; hearth space is covered by standing-money. Two westbound letters cost one copper apiece. [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 4]
28:- **The Quieting:** four sites lie on one straight edge of the map. The Ring, Stair and Hall were entered. The fourth was seen and paced from outside at **440 yards and two strides** radius, behind registry-iron stake 34 repeated one per pace. It is unentered, unnamed, undated and untested; its grey central upright is unresolved and its effect unknown. `Someone made this pattern.` was said once and not answered. [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 4]
