34:- **Cael:** nineteen, with **thirteen confirmed fragments**. Iron Wall came from Vastin in the Treswick alley (entered, **not told**; the debt stands; deployment none). Rune came from Cleon in the chamber (told to Cleon; the warning stands). Force came from Teague at the Span's barricade (first and only use on stone at the pass; the recoil stops in the ribs; never used on a person). **The still place** has been read by two instruments and understood by neither. Tide reads nothing, with everything going round it. Rune reads a shape with bones, a floor with nothing built on it. At the court's centre there was **no edge**: "Not the Quiet. Not a fragment. The same kind of made." **He told no one the Rune finding.** His Arbiter is dark and unchanged. The instruments read wrong in his hands and only his, with the **trend up** (a hair at Lowmarch; a stride short and "a hair and a half, two" at the plain's edge). That fact is unsourced. 123 marks; nothing owed.
36:- **Five sites lie on one bearing, ages ascending east.** The court is the fifth and the oldest, about 1,107 yards across, and the end of the line. [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 5] It is **unnamed** ("the court", lowercase). The taxonomy is decoded: a stroke alone, a stroke and bar, a stroke and two bars.
45:- **Cleon** stays under Treswick with the leaf and the board: "Work. Not a finding."
63:11. **KEEP — The slip (278th).** Clearance at the cut below the shoulder hold, twenty. "Ours" twice. Pike writes a sixth line for the healer. Vastin is not on the sheet and walks at the back.
64:12. **KEEP — The cut (279th).** Iron Wall is first shown: a plane across the road, rooted, and therefore loud. Brom fights silent with a rock. Lira works the scree. Cael bursts away, then goes still on the scree; the pack turns back and breaks on the wall. The heap. Seln in the heap. Five dead and three into the sink. Costs: Brom's foot; **Vastin's knee**, bound by Oryn for "a month". The lesson: "The wall held the line. And someone else had to be the reason they wanted the line." / "You do now." The log (§10).
65:13. **KEEP — The spring (280th).** Three readers: Karis for pattern, Seln for omission, Vastin for procedure. The office's instruments. **"Behaves as device. Cannot be."** Karis stops her lamps sentence with the ruler rule. **The grade:** the same stroke and bar on all four sites, the fourth's twice the size. "Two copies of one ignorance." Vastin's three reflexes: directive, classification, "This has to go up". The second row counts a sheet short in Cael's hands. Seln sets the technician's sheet before Cael without a word. Cael does the sum (the date matches his Kindling day; "six years" is the office's survey-record rounding; no numeric span since Kindling is computed [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 7]), does **not** write it down, and puts the sheet back. "You keep drafting orders." / "Habit." / "Out here the habit's the tell. Draft nothing. Just look." Cleon is named for the first time.
67:15. **KEEP — The last day of the road (281st).** Lira makes the same discipline of the crown, unasked. The reading inward, a fourth and fifth time: "a cord on a stone"; the instrument is wrong for a stillness. Vastin sits; "You were the instrument. I was the error." Vastin's confession, narrowed (ruling 18): "I declined to read you a second time. You know that. What you do not know is why." Cael gives him the instrument's nothing. It is not friendship; it is ground. The log (§10).
69:17. **KEEP — Cleon at noon (283rd).** "Off floors." / "Fifty-two sheets." His terms. He stops a step late.
70:18. **KEEP — The provision (284th).** Four hands go up by count: Cael, Brom, Lira and Vastin. Seln is not on the count. The square is avoided by Seln's route. The clerk does not ask and writes "four". **Lira's ladder does not pull** ("Four hands." / "Four." / "Right."). The iron door. Cleon pulls the iron to.
71:19. **KEEP — The Deepstacks (284th).** Cleon is already reading. The sheets are laid out 11/29/12. "Older than [UNBOUND]." "I know that hand." "Being believed … It's the end of being able to be wrong." "Give me a week." Cael is unfiled for the first time.
73:21. **KEEP — The marks (285th–287th).** The lamp trade. Cleon's board is matched to the Hall's fourth sheet: bearer, carried, ornament. "They're orders." **The limit**, verbatim. "Same make." Cael wants it turned on himself and does not say so. **Brom's yard:** he rights a cart with his back, no Path, is offered the life, and picks up the box on the bound shoulder. "Good. I'd hate to have turned down a real job for a wrong hunch." **Seln's night walk** from a roof below the walls: "I looked at it." Vastin: "How long did it take you." / "I was fourteen. I'm nineteen. I'm not there yet either." Cleon's close (§10). The 288th–289th are undramatized in the source.
75:23. **KEEP — The reader (291st).** By the carts' street in daylight. Cleon's inside: "An instruction leans … This is a stair." Karis: "The strata lean too." **Acquisition at "there".** Cael tells Lira first ("Twelfth. His. Lean."), then Cleon at the bell. "You did what." "That's not supposed to be possible. That's —" / "No. I'll not say that one." The cup of water; **the warning**. "He went back to the carving." Vastin and Cael take the case up together. The notice on the stair. The eyes are paid on the last flight. "Cael did not tell anyone. He remembered."
78:26. **KEEP — The yard fire (293rd evening).** Seln is told on the street ("Made." "For a kind."). Cleon comes up, the only time. **Lira first:** "So the whole time they weren't afraid you'd break something. They were afraid you'd *exist*." Brom's price. Seln keeps the cache "a while longer". Karis's two pages, then she falls asleep on a bucket. Brom to Cleon: "Good." Vastin: imperfect → corrupt → "aimed … At a category. Which turned out to be a person. Who's sitting across the fire." Lira: "You signed the mark at kindlings." / "I would have." **Pole two**, said aloud (§10). "I want to stand in the middle of it."
79:27. **KEEP — The list of parts (294th) and Cleon's goodbye at the bell:** "Work. Not a finding." / "Mind the stair. It leans."
82:30. **KEEP — The grade cracked (298th morning).** Three marks. Cleon's list puts the mark at the kindling and the mark on a sheet in one line: "A mark is a grade." Ages by first sheet: 61, 94, 138, 206. The third-tier point lies past the fourth, on the line. **Oldest-last.** "It's observation." **Vastin's first "Noted."** Teague: "Oldest last." / "Then that's where we're going." The log (§10).
89:37. **KEEP — The plain's edge (306th).** The burial at the east mouth by Teague's crew, with the six carrying at his leave. Lira and Seln recover the mule by the ridge path. **Eleven.** Oryn on the ribs: "Ribs. May I?" / "Yes." "That's a line. That's not yours." / "It's mine now." No term tonight. **Rune turned inward deliberately:** bones; a floor with nothing built on it; an instruction with no language; "the same kind of thing, to that instrument, as the sites were to Cleon's." Told to no one. The Arbiter unchanged. The instruments read wronger; the trend is up. The log (§10, "the whole year"). [OWNER-pending #58]
