145:- **Teague's wrist (flag):** the leather has been on it "since before the boy could lift a pack"; the joint is thicker than its fellow by the width of a finger; it "clicks"; "A Force paid where the line came out of him." The older healer binds it to her board at night and tells him to leave his Path shut till the thaw. A block lies on the second ledge of the cold road, with a herd lying up above it; he will shift it "as a carter would". The young one has brought him a hot cloth for it on every cold night since he joined. In his own window Teague is named as a Force for the first time in this edition. No Force is used on the page.
148:- **The kit as a tool (flag; as amended by the audit's five line fixes):** the cord is tarred hemp no thicker than a pencil, with a knot at every fifth stride and a brass eye whipped into one end; it is run out to its last knot, **the fourth**, and **"Four knots is a length"** (four five-stride intervals; no yardage is given anywhere); odd strides are taken with a notched slip of ash "a stride long by the dead man's reckoning". Karis cut a peg of peeled hazel to the stake's length. The inn yard, from the plank's left-hand post to a scratch on the stone trough by the gate: **"one length and four knots and two strides"**, forty-two; for Cael the slip laid once from the fourth knot leaves room for only half of it again. Karis measured the cord against the Ternhall brass on the 116th and again on the 170th: thirty-one lays "and a piece under half" to the first knot, unchanged, and the second, third and fourth knots the same.
150:- **Karis (flag):** her rule dates from the day, "as a girl", when a registrar laid her card before her and could not say what instrument it had been taken with. She once read the archive's name "on the spine of a catalogue that she was not allowed to open". The mark stands "beside the Stair twice over and beside the fourth place", and not beside the Fallow or the Hall (as Book 7's stakes have it). Her leaf: *What I should have to be able to show.*, eleven lines.
160:**Calendar.** The night of the **two hundred and seventieth day past the Line**, at Lowmarch. Days on the page: 131, 133, 138–146 (the fence; the herd on the 140th), 147, 148, 150, 158, 161, 168, 170 (Karis), 176, 190, 224, 230, 263, 264–265 (the saddle; the ford), 265–266 (Thornwater), 267–268 (down), 268, 270. No season, month or English weekday name is on the page. The river: shelf ice on the 131st; a road from the 154th; open at the middle on the 230th; "a week" from carrying a boat on the 268th; the scow's blocks being knocked out on the night of the 270th.
164:**Cael.** Nineteen. **Ten fragments.** **Deployment since the Line: twenty-nine** (twenty-seven at entry; the read on frozen ground at the calf, the 140th; the read on river ice, the 161st). All ten tried in the cold term and written up as *The ten, by use*: Wind (the lock cannot be shortened, only placed), Ember (the burn), Shadow (held, not opened), Compression (both heels; ground worth a load), Pressure (seen coming; narrow and deep; comes back), Blade (short; the steel pays), the read (ground or air; a pace and a half; the eyes), Storm (one lane; ten counts; a fourth untried), Anchor (a point held to thirty; ten, twelve and fourteen feet), Tide (asked of Lira; told no; not used). Shadow used twice in all and shut. Anchor's counted uses still two. Tide: Oryn twice, himself three times, nobody else. **The still place** has not been read or touched. **The instruments:** on the 168th the kit's cord (four knots to a length) measured the inn yard at forty-two strides for Karis, Lira, Brom and Seln and at forty-one and a piece for him, three times; the Ternhall brass read a hair short in his hand and Hesk's a hair long; he has touched none of the three since; his ruling is *hold*; Oryn has been told and has no answer. Nobody has offered a cause. He lost to Teague's spear three to none (148th) and three to one (158th). He has entered Teague as the better captain. He has not ruled on Karis's case. He has written *West, and inside*. Body: sound; knuckles skinned on the 140th; near sight lost for an hour on the 140th and for an evening on the 161st, and back.
170:**Karis.** Ember; Iron, Rank Three. **She has made her case to six** (the 268th): instructions; an index with a key that is kept; and then, in her protected speech, west, Treswick, the registry office on the old town, the Deepstacks under it, the old scholars' provision for a registered historical-studies practitioner, which she is not, and "a man there who is" (unnamed). She said the sentence whole to Cael on the 263rd, without the word west. She cannot read the four signs and has put no meaning on the stroke and the bar. She knows how the kit's cord is used and has taught the five. She has entered the anomaly as *Cause: not found. No inference entered.* and has written no sentence joining it to anything. Fifty-two sheets; the hide; the kit; the dead man's ledger, open now; a hair in her notebook. She keeps the purse.
174:**Oryn.** Tide; Iron, Rank Four. She released the arm only when Lira took it; mended the ankle; answered Lira's thanks with "Route's whole… The knee held. Nobody died of three weeks."; left the shoulder to the woman who tied it. She has seen the map with four rings and the line ("That's a line.") and has been told of the fourth site: twice the size, fenced, unentered. She has been told of the cord and the edges. **She has not read Cael** and has said that she will know what she is reading for before she does. At the word *station* she shut her mouth on a sentence and said nothing. She did not sit in the sixth place. She does not know that Seln is Shadow's source.
193:- **Cael and the fragments:** deployment is 29, not 27; the calf and river-ice reads are the two counted additions. Shadow remains exactly twice and sealed; Anchor's counted uses remain two; Tide was refused and unused; the still place remains untouched (`manuscript/chapter-02.md:225-229`; `manuscript/chapter-04.md:239-243`; `manuscript/chapter-05.md:211-217`; `manuscript/chapter-06.md:189-201`). His near sight recovered after both read bills, and his day-140 knuckles are old minor damage by day 270 (`manuscript/chapter-02.md:217-225`; `manuscript/chapter-04.md:191-209`).
198:- **Karis:** fifty-two sheets, map, two straightedges, kit, opened field ledger, one stored hair, and the eleven-line case remain under her control. She cannot read the four-sign index or know it is a grade; she has entered no causal theory (`manuscript/chapter-04.md:253-281`; `manuscript/chapter-05.md:145-195`; `manuscript/chapter-06.md:227-253`). After fix 14, *west* has now been spoken once at the day-268 table.
200:- **Oryn:** she knows the fourth-site description, the map line, and the instrument anomaly, but has not read Cael and will not until she knows the purpose (`manuscript/chapter-06.md:163-209`). She did not take the sixth chair (`manuscript/chapter-06.md:223-225`). Her grey jenny remains at Thornwater; the brown mule is with the six at Lowmarch (`book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-60.md:131-147`; `manuscript/chapter-06.md:65-77,217`).
202:- **Money, board, debts, and letters:** 118 living marks; sealed reserve untouched; eleven completed Pike lines; cloth still eleventh; sixty yards of four-strand rope owed for the first boat; one reed hurdle owed; Ephram's letter still due on the first boat; mule's cold-term shed fee paid (`manuscript/chapter-01.md:271`; `manuscript/chapter-03.md:295-299`; `manuscript/chapter-06.md:215-219,281-283`; `book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-60.md:75-91`).
205:**Movement 1 CLOSED (2026-10-11).** Sol recheck of repair r1: CLOSE WITH LINE FIXES; all four tracked passages RESOLVED against the source; no new tracking; every binding ruling above borne out by the surviving prose. Two fixes applied by the coordinator: ch3, the author's own "his Path" (of Teague) now reads "the Force"; ch6, Seln's sentence after Karis's protected speech now gives the asset-restriction as locked Book 6 ch58 states it — **the paper executes when an enrolled name is written in a book inside a district, and must be served within the hour** (not "a certificate inside the Line"). The "New canon minted" and "State at movement end" sections above were refreshed from the post-repair author report after the fixes. Final: 30,941 prose words; gates 0; overlap 0 unprotected (9 protected). Purse 118 marks; deployment twenty-nine; day 270 at Lowmarch.
208:## AFTER MOVEMENT 2 — chapters 7–12, days 271–277 (drafted 2026-10-11, author claude-opus-5-5, NO-SOURCE method)
213:- **Vastin** came over on the first boat on the 277th: a brown frieze coat, an ash stick, a bad knee, raw hands (the left does not open flat), a small purse; no age; **no Iron Wall shown** (he held the stern strap with a turn on a post, his boots and his back). He holds no office and nobody sent him. He has asked for a bed and for nothing else; he has not asked to join and nobody has framed him as joining. He sleeps in the loft over the tap.
215:- **The three papers.** (1) **The records:** a seat-courier's flat of waxed leather; six taped rows, a year to a row, of survey abstracts measured in lengths, knots and strides, with the dead surveyor's four-sign index printed at their heads; an **anomaly column** in which every sheet, in every hand, for six years carries the one word *Total* (an entry, not a sum; no figure); "More than four" (Karis, counting distinct sign-groups; she gives no number); the Fallow completion report is the last, loose sheet, and carries **five strokes for a name and a count of six** (locked Book 7 ch40, ch43), not five names. (2) **The page:** a COPY in Vastin's own hand of one line from an old register, carried in oilcloth in his coat: "—of the Architect: see the lower archive at Treswick, which holds it in full—". "The Architect" is a title, not a name, and a word Karis has never met in any stratum. It is never called a leaf; **the leaf has not appeared**. (3) **The technician's sheet:** the two protected lines with a date between them, a brush bar across what followed, and Karis's *not read*. **The date is a Compact date, a registry year and a day in it, and is never printed as figures** (the source gives none; no owner decision is needed). The office had filed the sheet at the end of the second row and it lies there again.
219:- **Cael has not touched the page.** He will rule at the plank in the morning (the 278th), in daylight, and ask for hands. Nobody said *west* in the back room.
220:- **Teague's spear** now has "he/his" on the page (OWNER-pending #59 stands as defaulted). Teague's wrist is unbound and unused; forty sacks of salt at the landing; whether he has left for the cold road is open.
226:All reads on Sol (gpt-5.6-sol): editorial; cold read; source-distance (1 tracked passage, ch12 scene 3; probe 2% / 12%, the excess being protected and plan-quoted document text); plan / canon / protected-text audit (REPAIR; 46 exact fixes, of which the coordinator applied 24 — protected units restored, two speakers corrected, "leaf" to "page" — and sent 22 to the author to recompose in voice). Coordinator rulings against the audit: the technician's date is NOT owner-pending (the source prints no value; the page shows a date and no figures); the completion report carries five strokes, not five names (Book 7 ch43:51), where the audit's fix kept "five names". **Repair r1 in progress with the same author.**
239:- **Vastin as he arrives (flag):** a drover's coat of brown frieze, too short in the sleeve, bought "at the last market inside the Line"; the grey one left on its hook; an ash stick cut out of a hedge; a pack with one strap mended in cord; a small purse on a cord; the flat carried under the pack against his back, and **a single copied page** inside his coat in oilcloth. **The knee** "had begun to complain at about the hundredth mile and had left off being civil at the two hundredth"; no side is given; ten miles a day. He left "the seal of his office in the tray marked *done*, some months ago, on a morning of rain, with nothing written to go beside it". At the last station he looks in at the plate and remembers only what Book 5 shows: a plate, a file and a set of questions carried up a bluff, "and all three had told him nothing"; and that he declined a second reading and never said why. He crossed the sill on the 265th and reached the western landing on the evening of the 276th. His left hand would not open after the strap and has not lain flat since. He has paid a copper for the fare, a copper and a half for a loaf, a copper for a bowl and a copper for the loft. He sleeps in **the loft over the tap, up the keeper's stair**.
240:- **What Vastin adds about the layer (repaired: four facts and no more).** (1) It cannot be reached: he asked to be shown what the office holds upon the thing beneath the function; "The office has one page upon the matter, and it is the office's own. The page says that the layer is not to be opened; and it gives as its reason that it cannot be"; it "reserves no leave to anybody". (2) The citation: in the oldest register of housings that he was let to see, the line for the layer has no maker's name but a word and a place. (3) The held records (the flat). (4) The technician's line. **Cut in repair:** the frame-shop mender, the shimmed frame, the rule of the shop, the office's schedules, and any history of attempts. He could not go to the archive himself: an archive on the Line keeps a book at its door. Brom and Lira say what it changes: "So there's nobody to ask"; "it'll not be the people who own the plates that tell him."
243:- **The page (repaired): a copy.** One sheet of the house's plain desk paper, folded twice, in Vastin's own square upright hand, in fresh ink. He copied the line "from a record that is older than the section it is filed in, in a room where I had the right to read and no right to copy", with the word and the place "exactly as they are written there, letter for letter", and the schedule of housings round it (a number, a date of setting and a mender's mark to each) to show where the line falls. He read the pages on both sides and did not copy them. **No cut edge, no blade, no inquiry, and no prompt from the ninth fragment.**
245:- **Karis's receipt (repaired), 12:173:** *Received of Vastin, at Lowmarch, day two hundred and seventy-seven past the Line: one courier's flat, holding six rows of abstracts in their tapes, one row looked through and no sheet counted; one broker's report; one page, copied by him from a register; one technician's sheet, copied by me this night and laid back in the second row. Read in part. Understood in no part. — K.*
250:**Calendar.** The night of the **two hundred and seventy-seventh day past the Line**, at Lowmarch. Days on the page: 271, 272, 273, 275, 276, 277; Vastin's window, 265–276. No season, month or English weekday name is on the page.
254:**Cael.** Nineteen. **Ten fragments.** **Deployment since the Line: thirty** (the read on the ground at the landing, the 277th). Shadow used twice in all and shut; held at dusk on the 272nd and the 277th. Anchor's counted uses still two. Tide: Oryn twice, himself three times, nobody else; he did not ask to read the knee. **The still place** has not been read, touched or named. He has not touched the cord or either brass edge for a hundred and nine days; the ruling is *hold*. His near sight went at the landing and was back for print by the afternoon. **He has not ruled.** He will say it "at the plank in the morning, in daylight" and ask for hands. He has not touched the copied page; his hand lay a hand's width from it for the whole of a lamp. **He has not read the technician's date**: he was at the table's far end; he knows that it is a registry year and a day, and that it is the line at which Seln stopped; he chose not to go up the table and read it. He lost the bout to Lira, two touches to three. He has written to Ephram. He kept back his own question to Vastin (why the second reading was declined). He has told Vastin nothing of what he carries.
258:**Brom.** Iron Skin; Copper. No declaration; no grey at the landing. **Right shoulder still in the older healer's webbing**; she pressed the knot on the 272nd and went away. He shored the post with a timber on the left shoulder. He has the purse; a hundred and eighteen. He roped the three boxes for carrying on the night of the 277th.
260:**Karis.** Ember; Iron, Rank Three. Her case stands "not by a line" altered. She holds, received and receipted: **the flat, with six rows in their tapes (one row looked through; no sheet counted) and the technician's sheet laid back at the foot of the second row; the broker's completion report; Vastin's copied page**, which lies on its oilcloth at the bare end of her table; and **her own exact copy of the technician's sheet**, with the office's date figures as they stand, a ruled box and *not read* in it, and a note of where the sheet lies. She has said that the word on the page is a title and not a name, that she has never met it in any stratum, and nothing more. She has said "More than four" and no number. She has seen *Total* in the anomaly column on every sheet she turned, in the newest row and the oldest. She cannot read the index; it is an office's index now and not only the dead man's. She has connected nothing to anything. She keeps the lamp.
266:**Vastin.** No office, no seal, no rank; he left the seal in a tray "some months" ago and walked three hundred miles. **No age is stated.** A bad knee; raw hands; a left hand that will not lie flat. **No Iron Wall has been shown or named.** He has handed over three things in his own order and holds Karis's receipt in his coat. He has said: that he holds no office and has no sanction; that the layer cannot be opened ("There is no key"), on the authority of the office's own page; that the one line which should name its maker cites a title and sends its reader to Treswick's lower archive (his own copy of it); that nothing of his follows him and the Stair's rim is not his; that the pending paper is unchanged; why he did not take it to a council. He knows the six by name. **He does not know** the mechanism, what Cael carries, the instruments' behaviour in Cael's hand, Karis's case or the sites (beyond hearing Brom say "four on the hide" and Lira name the Stair), who held the abstracts, which classification event the sheet means, or what is under the bar. He has not weighed the sheet's date. He has not read the flat's last row through, and nothing has been said of a directive or an objection. He has not asked to join and nobody has spoken of it. He was sent to bed, began to argue twice, took four stairs fast and the rest slowly; whether that was the order or the knee is not settled.
272:**Objects and money.** **A hundred and eighteen marks in hand**, unchanged. The reserve sealed. Owed: **sixty yards of four-strand rope** to the ferryman (the cordage is on the western landing; his one hauling rope has two yarns gone). **The hurdle is paid.** **The letter to Ephram is sent.** The three boxes are at the hearth's end, roped. Stake thirty-two has still never been driven. On Karis's table: the flat (the sheet inside it), the broker's paper beside it, Seln's wand beside that, and the copied page at the far end.
278:**Words said aloud for the first time.** *Vastin* (Seln, at the landing). *Treswick* by Vastin, at noon, from the other side. On paper only, and said by nobody: the title on the page. Not said aloud by anybody in chapters 10–12: *west*.
280:**Open threads.** A ruling to be given at the plank in the morning. A page that Cael has not touched. A date that stopped Seln and that Cael has not read. A bar with something under it. A count that Karis has not checked. A paper that came to a desk with no routing note. A sentence that a healer has swallowed three times. A knee that nobody has asked about. A man in a loft with a receipt and nothing to do. A rope on the wrong bank. A captain's term with no day in it. A question that Cael kept.
283:Packet 003 already carries day 278, the clearance slip, Vastin at the door end and not on the sheet, the silent drill, the cut, the spring, the date sum, the fork and days 279–281 (`packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:20–38`). Its author must additionally inherit:
285:- **Paper custody and exact positions.** Karis holds the courier's flat, six taped rows, the completion report, Vastin's copied page, the technician's sheet, and her exact copy with the ruled box and *not read* (`manuscript/chapter-12.md:3–15,59–65,101–135,157–169`). At the close (as repaired), the flat and the completion report are under the lamp; the original technician's sheet lies back at the end of the second row, where the office had filed it, and Karis has noted its place beneath her copy; the copied page is on oilcloth at the bare far end. Vastin holds Karis's unsealed receipt inside the brown coat (`manuscript/chapter-12.md:157–175`). Seln's forty-seven-notch wand lies under the lamp beside the broker's sheet; he will cut no forty-eighth (`manuscript/chapter-12.md:251–255`).
288:- **Bodies and equipment.** Lira's arm will be on day 13 out of wool on day 278, still slow and wet-aching; her ankle is sound in the large boot (`manuscript/chapter-06.md:127–151`; `manuscript/chapter-08.md:3–5,71–135,147`). Brom's right shoulder remains in the older healer's knot (`manuscript/chapter-07.md:173–183`). The three boxes are roped tight for carrying with beckets out (`manuscript/chapter-12.md:243–249,281–283`). Seln's locked case remains shut (`manuscript/chapter-11.md:191–199`; `packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:37`).
290:- **Ledger state.** It is the night before day 278; crew purse 118 marks; deployment thirty; ten fragments; Shadow still sealed after two prior uses; Anchor still two counted uses; Tide unused here; still place untouched (`manuscript/chapter-08.md:151–153`; `manuscript/chapter-09.md:263–265`; `manuscript/chapter-12.md:291–295`). Cael has not touched the page and has promised a daylight ruling at the plank with hands (`manuscript/chapter-12.md:223–241,267–299`).
292:**Movement 2 CLOSED (2026-10-11).** Same-author repair r1: the 24 coordinator-applied fixes kept and their joins smoothed; the page made a copy; the layer cut to four facts (Lira and Brom say what it changes: there is nobody to ask); *Total* made the anomaly column's entry; the technician's sheet read out by Lira with a date and no figures, filed at and laid back at the end of the second row; Seln's stillness re-entered in a new order; receipt and night log made literally true ("Read in part. Understood in no part."); the completion report's five strokes and count of six; ch7's opening oriented. Sol recheck: CLOSE WITH LINE FIXES; the tracked passage RESOLVED; every binding ruling above borne out; the day arithmetic confirmed (ice 111 days; the wrist 124; the sling 170; the rim 163; the cord 109; the report 175). Three fixes applied by the coordinator: ch7 "a healer's Path" → "a healer's craft" (no possessive before Path in narration); ch8's bluff memory cut back to what Book 5 shows; ch10 "through a frame shop" removed. Rulings from the recheck: **Lira reading the sheet aloud is the author's staging and stands** (the map protects the wording, the sum and the withholding, not the reader); the two descriptions of the cited record agree. The "New canon minted" and "State at movement end" sections above were refreshed from the post-repair author report. Final: 30,105 prose words; gates 0; overlap 0 unprotected (11 protected). Purse 118 marks; deployment thirty; the night before day 278 at Lowmarch.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-009.md:10:> **[Coordinator rulings after the Movement 1 audit, 2026-10-11 — binding; they override any plan text below that differs.]** (1) **Teague's spear is a tall MAN** (he / him): the locked Book 7 wrote him so (ch25, ch51, ch52), and Book 8 follows its own edition (OWNER-pending #59). Where the plan says "the tall woman", read "the tall man"; his silence toward the six until his question at the pass stands. (2) **Teague can read** (locked Book 7 ch25: he read a slip twice). Never write that he cannot; if he does not read a sheet it is because it is not in front of him or he has no need. (3) **Lira's asking:** she asked Oryn once about the ankle on the mountain in Book 7 and asked nobody for anything from then until Thornwater; do not call Thornwater her first ask since Norhold. (4) **The stroke and bar** is on stake thirty-two (the Stair's newer stake and the kit's unused one) and on the fourth site's thirty-four ONLY; stakes thirty-one and thirty-three do not carry it. Later records may show the grade on survey SHEETS; the field stakes do not all carry it. (5) **The cord:** the kit's cord is twenty strides, knotted at the fives (four knots to a length); Book 7's Ring was sixty-two cords and twenty strides round. The court is about 1,107 yards across, which is about FIFTY cords, not 159. Give no yardage for a cord. (6) **"West"** was first said aloud at the six-person table on the 268th (Karis's protected "It's west… Treswick…" speech, printed once in ch6). (7) **Deployment since the Line is twenty-nine** at the end of Movement 1 (two uses of the Iron read in earnest); trials are not counted.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-009.md:12:> **[Coordinator rulings after the Movement 2 audit, 2026-10-11 — binding; they override any plan text below that differs.]** (1) **Vastin's second paper is "the page": a COPY in his own hand** of one line from an old register ("—of the Architect: see the lower archive at Treswick, which holds it in full—"). It was never cut from anything and is never called a leaf; "the leaf" is the chamber record of Movement 6 only. (2) **The technician's sheet carries a Compact date (a registry year and a day in it) that is NEVER printed as figures** anywhere in this book; whoever reads it reads a date, and the page does not give its numbers. The office filed that sheet at the end of the second row of the records, and it lies there. (3) **The anomaly column:** on every survey abstract, in every hand, for six years, the entry is the one word *Total* — an entry, not a sum. (4) **The Fallow completion report** carries five strokes for a name and a count of six (locked Book 7), not five written names. (5) **What Vastin has told the six about the layer is four things only:** no key (it cannot be reached); the citation; the suppressed records; the technician's line. He has not defined "classification event" and does not know which event is meant. Nothing on the page says that menders, technicians or any office have tried to open it or know more. (6) **Speakers:** "What follows you," was Lira's; "She's right. Go and lie down, and don't take the stairs fast," was Oryn's. (7) **Deployment since the Line is thirty** at the end of Movement 2 (the Iron read at the landing on the 277th). Purse 118 marks. (8) **Teague's spear** has "he/his" on the page from chapter 7 (OWNER-pending #59 as defaulted). (9) Vastin has shown no Iron Wall, has no stated age, has asked only for a bed, and holds Karis's unsealed receipt. Cael has not touched the page and has not read the sheet's date closely.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-009.md:19:  - From `BOOK_MAP.md`: §1 Ending; §2 items 36–40; §3 A (the pass), C (burial; pacing); §5 (the Seln, Oryn and Vastin cutaways); §7.1 (the Force first use; Rune inward; the still place; the instruments; the Arbiter); §8 (the pass); §9; §10 Tier A 19–22 and the S21–S24 Tier C lines, including the closing prose; **§11**; §12 C3, C11; §13; §15.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-009.md:24:It is first light on the 306th, at the shale camp below the notch. Seln comes back wet to the ankle from the pass's floor. Twelve and a mule. Vastin is on day 27. The ribs have been quiet since the marsh, and the thirteenth is listening.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-009.md:28:The book's cost, then its answer. The pass takes a life that did not have to be lost and that the found family can only witness. That night the second instrument is turned inward on purpose, and the still place reads as made. At the end of the line, at the oldest floor, Cael walks alone to the centre. There is no edge there and no seam, and he fits. He does not say the third sentence. Everyone takes their own road home.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-009.md:32:  - Seln's reconnaissance. "It's through." Cael draws it and tells the doctrine to Teague's four, once: "Behind it. Noted?" / "Noted." The young one nods with his whole head.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-009.md:34:  - The wall goes up as a lean-to slant. Brom's forearm is bolted before it is up.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-009.md:36:  - The broad man is hit at the slant's high edge. **The young one goes out a stride to drag him and is killed by the sixth volley.** Oryn's hands are on him, and come off with nothing done. Vastin cannot move. The broad man says the name, once. [OWNER-pending #54]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-009.md:37:  - Seln goes over the lip at the seventh volley. **Cael's first use of Force** on the second stack's brace, taking it along the shelf. The recoil stops in the ribs.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-009.md:39:  - Vastin goes down. Karis sits with her bound hand on his shoulder. Teague kneels by his own dead. **"A wall keeps everyone behind it, and one of mine wasn't."** At the far mouth Cael understands that the line was not drawn in ink.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-009.md:40:- **Burial and the plain's edge (306th).** Teague's crew builds the cairn in their own order. The six carry at his leave. Lira and Seln recover the mule by the ridge path. **Eleven.** Oryn: "Ribs. May I?" / "Yes." **"That's a line. That's not yours." / "It's mine now."** No term tonight.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-009.md:41:- **The still place, read as made (~3,000).** He recalls the warning by heart. Then **the twelfth turned inward on purpose**: still; set; *bones*; *a floor with nothing built on it*; *an instruction with no language*. "The same kind of thing, to that instrument, as the sites were to Cleon's." He tells no one, not Lira, not Oryn, not Karis. The Arbiter is unchanged. **The instruments read wronger**: the cord a stride short, the edges a hair and a half to two out. The trend is up and he draws no line. **The log, verbatim** ("the whole year"). [OWNER-pending #58]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-009.md:42:- **The court (307th; ~6,000).** It lies low on the plain, and the rock is worn to the floor for a mile. The stumps. **The pacing: about fifty cords** [M1 audit: not 159; the kit's cord is twenty strides, knotted at the fives], Lira on the line, about 1,107 yards across [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: OWNER-pending #48; coordinator ruling], sharp and perfect. The cuts are deeper, there is a stratum under everything, and this is the first cut: "The others are copies." The bearing ends, with no sixth site. The log is written standing. The council: the same three sentences as the crest, and one more.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-009.md:43:- **At the line (dusk).** Every sigil goes dark at the same stride. Lira: "Right." Brom prices the stump. Karis: "It's the first one." Seln gives the count. Vastin: "This is where they drew it." Oryn steps in one stride and back: "Nothing. Everything, round it. Same as you." It goes unanswered. Teague steps in one stride and back: "Field's mine. This isn't field." The turning begins. **The fixed exchange, then "Wait here."**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-009.md:45:- **The line again.** Oryn: "May I?" / "Yes." "The same finding." Lira: "Well?" / "I'll tell you on the road. If there's road." He tells nobody what the centre felt like and gives them the count instead. "Twenty-nine tomorrow." / "Thirty's the month."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-009.md:46:- **The ledger, the letter and the dawn (307th night–308th), verbatim.** Teague: "After the next thaw … My crew comes." [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: OWNER-pending #48] Oryn: "The day I have to." … "After the thaw: bring the map, and lie still when I say." [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: OWNER-pending #48] "Six. Six and no mule." Vastin is unadmitted. "West." **Closing prose, verbatim.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-009.md:49:**Cutaways (~5,800):** Seln, ~1,800, on the ridge with Lira to recover the mule: the swept scree below, the dead pine. Oryn, ~2,000, the night after the first death under her hands. **She has not heard the leaf. No cutaway at the court.** Vastin, ~2,000, at the court's rim at night: the line he never asked about. **He is unadmitted and not asking. There is no hint of Book 9's request.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-009.md:50:**Development:** about 15 Cael beats. Supporting: Teague 2, Oryn 2, Lira 2, Vastin 2, Karis 1–2, Seln 1–2, Brom 1.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-009.md:54:- **There is no word for what Cael is.** Never "recurrence", "primordial", "before" or "source". No tomb. "The court" stays lowercase and descriptive.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-009.md:59:- Vastin does not ask and is not asked; there is no vote. Oryn has not heard the leaf. Cael is nineteen.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-009.md:60:- Count Oryn's days past her road from the cairn (§12 C3). The letter's "Tell Lira's family I said so" stays verbatim (§12 C11). [OWNER-pending #55]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:10:> **[Coordinator rulings after the Movement 1 audit, 2026-10-11 — binding; they override any plan text below that differs.]** (1) **Teague's spear is a tall MAN** (he / him): the locked Book 7 wrote him so (ch25, ch51, ch52), and Book 8 follows its own edition (OWNER-pending #59). Where the plan says "the tall woman", read "the tall man"; his silence toward the six until his question at the pass stands. (2) **Teague can read** (locked Book 7 ch25: he read a slip twice). Never write that he cannot; if he does not read a sheet it is because it is not in front of him or he has no need. (3) **Lira's asking:** she asked Oryn once about the ankle on the mountain in Book 7 and asked nobody for anything from then until Thornwater; do not call Thornwater her first ask since Norhold. (4) **The stroke and bar** is on stake thirty-two (the Stair's newer stake and the kit's unused one) and on the fourth site's thirty-four ONLY; stakes thirty-one and thirty-three do not carry it. Later records may show the grade on survey SHEETS; the field stakes do not all carry it. (5) **The cord:** the kit's cord is twenty strides, knotted at the fives (four knots to a length); Book 7's Ring was sixty-two cords and twenty strides round. The court is about 1,107 yards across, which is about FIFTY cords, not 159. Give no yardage for a cord. (6) **"West"** was first said aloud at the six-person table on the 268th (Karis's protected "It's west… Treswick…" speech, printed once in ch6). (7) **Deployment since the Line is twenty-nine** at the end of Movement 1 (two uses of the Iron read in earnest); trials are not counted.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:12:> **[Coordinator rulings after the Movement 2 audit, 2026-10-11 — binding; they override any plan text below that differs.]** (1) **Vastin's second paper is "the page": a COPY in his own hand** of one line from an old register ("—of the Architect: see the lower archive at Treswick, which holds it in full—"). It was never cut from anything and is never called a leaf; "the leaf" is the chamber record of Movement 6 only. (2) **The technician's sheet carries a Compact date (a registry year and a day in it) that is NEVER printed as figures** anywhere in this book; whoever reads it reads a date, and the page does not give its numbers. The office filed that sheet at the end of the second row of the records, and it lies there. (3) **The anomaly column:** on every survey abstract, in every hand, for six years, the entry is the one word *Total* — an entry, not a sum. (4) **The Fallow completion report** carries five strokes for a name and a count of six (locked Book 7), not five written names. (5) **What Vastin has told the six about the layer is four things only:** no key (it cannot be reached); the citation; the suppressed records; the technician's line. He has not defined "classification event" and does not know which event is meant. Nothing on the page says that menders, technicians or any office have tried to open it or know more. (6) **Speakers:** "What follows you," was Lira's; "She's right. Go and lie down, and don't take the stairs fast," was Oryn's. (7) **Deployment since the Line is thirty** at the end of Movement 2 (the Iron read at the landing on the 277th). Purse 118 marks. (8) **Teague's spear** has "he/his" on the page from chapter 7 (OWNER-pending #59 as defaulted). (9) Vastin has shown no Iron Wall, has no stated age, has asked only for a bed, and holds Karis's unsealed receipt. Cael has not touched the page and has not read the sheet's date closely.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:16:> Packet 003 already carries day 278, the clearance slip, Vastin at the door end and not on the sheet, the silent drill, the cut, the spring, the date sum, the fork and days 279–281 (`packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:20–38`). Its author must additionally inherit:
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:18:> - **Paper custody and exact positions.** Karis holds the courier's flat, six taped rows, the completion report, Vastin's copied page, the technician's sheet, and her exact copy with the ruled box and *not read* (`manuscript/chapter-12.md:3–15,59–65,101–135,157–169`). At the close (as repaired), the flat and the completion report are under the lamp; the original technician's sheet lies back at the end of the second row, where the office had filed it, and Karis has noted its place beneath her copy; the copied page is on oilcloth at the bare far end. Vastin holds Karis's unsealed receipt inside the brown coat (`manuscript/chapter-12.md:157–175`). Seln's forty-seven-notch wand lies under the lamp beside the broker's sheet; he will cut no forty-eighth (`manuscript/chapter-12.md:251–255`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:19:> - **What each knows.** All six and Vastin have heard no key, the citation/title/place, suppressed survey records and the technician's visible line/bar (`manuscript/chapter-10.md:149–193`; `manuscript/chapter-11.md:201–257`; `manuscript/chapter-12.md:59–151`). Karis has not finished the records and cannot read the index or bar (`manuscript/chapter-11.md:223–253`; `manuscript/chapter-12.md:129–135,285–289`). Seln has done an unexplained sum and said only “I have read it”; Cael does not know the sum (`manuscript/chapter-12.md:137–153`). Vastin does not know the integration mechanism, directive, objection, what Cael carries, or what lies under the bar (`manuscript/chapter-10.md:129–131`; `manuscript/chapter-12.md:119–129`). Nobody connects the date to anyone (`manuscript/chapter-12.md:137–153`). Oryn has not read Cael and has not asked to read Vastin's knee (`manuscript/chapter-11.md:29–47`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:20:> - **Vastin's physical state and status.** Brown frieze coat, ash stick, bad knee, raw hands and a left hand that does not open flat; no age; no Iron Wall shown; not joined and has asked only for a bed (`manuscript/chapter-08.md:197–201`; `manuscript/chapter-09.md:115–143,187–191`; `manuscript/chapter-10.md:231–271`; `manuscript/chapter-11.md:19–23`). He sleeps in the loft over the tap, up the keeper's stair, after beginning the climb fast and finishing slowly (`manuscript/chapter-10.md:263–271`; `manuscript/chapter-12.md:193–219,297`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:21:> - **Bodies and equipment.** Lira's arm will be on day 13 out of wool on day 278, still slow and wet-aching; her ankle is sound in the large boot (`manuscript/chapter-06.md:127–151`; `manuscript/chapter-08.md:3–5,71–135,147`). Brom's right shoulder remains in the older healer's knot (`manuscript/chapter-07.md:173–183`). The three boxes are roped tight for carrying with beckets out (`manuscript/chapter-12.md:243–249,281–283`). Seln's locked case remains shut (`manuscript/chapter-11.md:191–199`; `packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:37`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:23:> - **Ledger state.** It is the night before day 278; crew purse 118 marks; deployment thirty; ten fragments; Shadow still sealed after two prior uses; Anchor still two counted uses; Tide unused here; still place untouched (`manuscript/chapter-08.md:151–153`; `manuscript/chapter-09.md:263–265`; `manuscript/chapter-12.md:291–295`). Cael has not touched the page and has promised a daylight ruling at the plank with hands (`manuscript/chapter-12.md:223–241,267–299`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:35:It is the morning of the 278th day. A new slip is pinned on Pike's plank: *Clearance. The cut below the shoulder hold, on the border road, two days west.* It pays twenty. Nobody has said Treswick aloud since the page. Vastin sits at the door end and is not on the sheet.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:39:West is decided as a job, not a vow. The first fight shows the reader Iron Wall, and its cost, in a man who has only ever stood. On the road the records are read three ways at once. Cael does a sum and does not write it down. The healer routes north with a promise written in the log. This is still the first third, so the progression teaching stays dense: Iron Wall's mechanics and limits, the silent doctrine, the office's grade.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:42:- **The slip:** "Ours" (Karis), then "Ours" (Brom). Pike writes a sixth line for the healer. Vastin follows.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:43:- **Road day one (278th, ~2,000):** a silent-movement drill for the newcomer. Walk silent, signal by hand, nobody declares unless they are meant to be loud. Vastin walks at the back of the column, where a man walks who has not been told where to walk. He is learning the doctrine, not drilling under a wall (§13).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:44:- **The cut (279th, ~3,500–4,000, developed).** Scout it from the lip first. The factor: "Carters declare, on the ice." Positions as in BOOK_MAP §8. **Iron Wall first shown:** a plane across the road, wall to wall. It holds eight hounds at a run, but the man holding it is rooted and becomes the loudest thing in the cut. Brom works its south end silent with a rock. Lira works the scree with two arms. Cael bursts *away*, then goes still on the scree while the lock beat lands. The pack turns back and breaks on the wall. The heap; Seln in the heap; the runnel; steel. Five dead and three into the sink ("clear because it's empty, not because it's safe"). Costs: Brom's foot. **Vastin's knee**, bound by Oryn for "a month". The lesson, verbatim, and the log, verbatim.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:45:- **The spring (280th).** Three readers. The instruments. **"Behaves as device. Cannot be."** Karis stops her lamps sentence with the ruler rule. **The grade:** the same stroke and bar on all four sites, the fourth's twice the size; "Two copies of one ignorance." Vastin has three reflexes: a directive, a classification, "This has to go up". The second row counts a sheet short in Cael's hands. **Seln sets the technician's sheet before Cael.** Cael does the sum: the date matches his Kindling day; no numeric elapsed span is computed [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 21]. He does not write it, and puts the sheet back. Then: "You keep drafting orders." / "Habit." / "Out here the habit's the tell. Draft nothing. Just look." This is the first thing Seln has ever taught anyone. **Close, verbatim:** Cleon is named for the first time.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:46:- **The fork-stone (280th evening).** Oryn's terms: "I'm not an archive person." The city she left; the column for the patient's tier; "Leaving and routing are different verbs." "Three weeks." **The station term:** she asks for it, he writes it in the log and reads it back, verbatim. She prices everyone, Vastin included and none priced lower than the rest. Millrace: "Bring me whatever walks out of that archive with you. All of it."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:47:- **First light (281st).** "Not the steps. Not the square." The mule goes north with Oryn. Cael turns at a quarter-mile. From the top of the rise he sees Treswick, and a pale steady light on its crown that he does not look at.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:50:**Cutaway (~1,800):** Seln at the spring. He does the sum and decides to set the sheet in front of Cael without a word. He weighs what it costs to give a thing without saying it. He does not theorize about the deep layer. **Seln's locked case stays shut, unopened and undecided.** [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 21]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:51:**Development:** about 15 Cael beats. Supporting: Vastin 3, Seln 2, Oryn 2, Karis 2, Brom 1, Lira 1.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:55:- The Iron Wall shown here is Vastin's. **Cael does not acquire it here.** The eleventh comes in the alley (Movement 5).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:56:- The deep-layer arithmetic is Cael's and Seln's alone. It is never spoken or written, and **never interpreted**.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:58:- Vastin's age is not stated. Oryn does not read Cael; "the one thing I'm walking up that road owing".
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:64:The drill's details and Vastin's mistakes in it. Exactly how the pack moves on ice. How long the scouting takes. The spring's light and wind. The order in which the three readers find things. How Oryn prices each of them, and the fork's last fire. Whether Vastin's three reflexes come in one scene or across the halt.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:68:A city stands on a bluff ahead, with three walls in tiers and a light on its crown. A healer's term is written in the log. A man on a stick has learned one sentence from a defector, and a boy carries a date he will not write down. Five people and a marshal walk toward the first registry Cael has ever gone to on purpose.
