editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:20:  - From `BOOK_MAP.md`: §2 items 32–35; §3 A (the Span; water at the seep), B 6, C (the leg); §5 (the Seln, Teague and Karis cutaways); §8 (the Span); §9; §10 Tier A 7–8, 14, 26 and the S19–S20 Tier C lines; §11; §12 C3, C14; §13.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:25:It is dawn on the 299th, at Millrace ford. There are twelve and a mule. Teague's wrist is wrapped. Vastin is on day 20. Karis is writing with the bound hand. Oryn's road runs east with them for a day and a half and then it does not.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:29:The leg goes on the page as the place where two crews learn each other, and where the young one becomes someone a reader will grieve. Then the fourth site: a watch-post, a barricade, a captain's line, and a width that wins because the people inside the line have stood there before, with nothing gained by it. The thirteenth arrives. The next night every finding goes onto one blanket, the lamps finding is said aloud and filed on its own page, and a marshal finds a crack he does not pry.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:35:  - The Hall's marsh, where Cael read himself twice earlier at the Hall. [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 26]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:37:  - "Known" is entered under each date. The crest at dusk on the 303rd.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:38:- **The crest.** The watch-post: hut, fire, kit under a hide, two timbers, seven hoods, two crossbows, one low practitioner. "They knew." Seln: "That iron's been in the ground years. Not one cold term." [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: OWNER-pending #48] Teague: "Drawn?" Cael draws it. "Nobody declares. Nobody dies. They're seven people on a posting. Noted?" / Teague's **first "Noted."**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:40:  1. The watch has the first exchange. Brom takes bolts on Iron.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:41:  2. **Teague goes through the middle.** Cael is at his left, a stride back, the whole exchange. **The thirteenth.** The notice renders verbatim. The recoil goes to the wrist, then the elbow: "Through."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:42:  3. The watch reforms. **"Nothing was gained inside" is entered first.** "By count." Five go over stake thirty-four (Cael, then Lira, Karis, the young one, Vastin) and four stay on the shelf. They walk. The pinch. Eleven seconds. "You'll die in there." / "We've been in three times." The watch goes east one at a time and is not pursued.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:45:  **Win sentence, verbatim.** Oryn sets and knits the leg and is grey for a quarter-hour. The healers nod. Teague's arm: "That's a fact about a line." / "Noted" / "Everybody says that now." Brom's week of colours.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:48:  - **The lamps finding, verbatim.** Vastin: "If a man designed the apparatus, then the sigils —" / the ruler rule. Two pages. Vastin's third "Noted." **Cael does not add his own third page.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:51:  - **Force, dry:** Cael lines his frame on the shale without firing. The thirteenth listens and the ribs warn him.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:56:**Development:** about 15 Cael beats. Supporting: Teague 2, the young one 2, Karis 2, Vastin 2, Seln 1–2, Oryn 2, Brom 1, Lira 1.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:62:- Teague is **not told** Cael took his Force. The Force is not used, only lined dry. "First use" belongs to the pass.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:63:- The two pages stay separate in every head. Never use *terminal*, *circuit* or *infrastructure*. "Recent administration" means **the Compact**. Nobody reaches for "someone else".
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:73:A notch in the hills to the east, low and square, where the bearing runs. Seln did not like it and will look again from nearer. Past it, by the office's distance, the oldest site waits. Cael wants it more than anything since he was fourteen, and he has told Karis why. He was right. He does not yet know how right.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:7:- Word budget: ~32,000
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:10:> **[Coordinator rulings after the Movement 1 audit, 2026-10-11 — binding; they override any plan text below that differs.]** (1) **Teague's spear is a tall MAN** (he / him): the locked Book 7 wrote him so (ch25, ch51, ch52), and Book 8 follows its own edition (OWNER-pending #59). Where the plan says "the tall woman", read "the tall man"; his silence toward the six until his question at the pass stands. (2) **Teague can read** (locked Book 7 ch25: he read a slip twice). Never write that he cannot; if he does not read a sheet it is because it is not in front of him or he has no need. (3) **Lira's asking:** she asked Oryn once about the ankle on the mountain in Book 7 and asked nobody for anything from then until Thornwater; do not call Thornwater her first ask since Norhold. (4) **The stroke and bar** is on stake thirty-two (the Stair's newer stake and the kit's unused one) and on the fourth site's thirty-four ONLY; stakes thirty-one and thirty-three do not carry it. Later records may show the grade on survey SHEETS; the field stakes do not all carry it. (5) **The cord:** the kit's cord is twenty strides, knotted at the fives (four knots to a length); Book 7's Ring was sixty-two cords and twenty strides round. The court is about 1,107 yards across, which is about FIFTY cords, not 159. Give no yardage for a cord. (6) **"West"** was first said aloud at the six-person table on the 268th (Karis's protected "It's west… Treswick…" speech, printed once in ch6). (7) **Deployment since the Line is twenty-nine** at the end of Movement 1 (two uses of the Iron read in earnest); trials are not counted.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:12:> **[Coordinator rulings after the Movement 2 audit, 2026-10-11 — binding; they override any plan text below that differs.]** (1) **Vastin's second paper is "the page": a COPY in his own hand** of one line from an old register ("—of the Architect: see the lower archive at Treswick, which holds it in full—"). It was never cut from anything and is never called a leaf; "the leaf" is the chamber record of Movement 6 only. (2) **The technician's sheet carries a Compact date (a registry year and a day in it) that is NEVER printed as figures** anywhere in this book; whoever reads it reads a date, and the page does not give its numbers. The office filed that sheet at the end of the second row of the records, and it lies there. (3) **The anomaly column:** on every survey abstract, in every hand, for six years, the entry is the one word *Total* — an entry, not a sum. (4) **The Fallow completion report** carries five strokes for a name and a count of six (locked Book 7), not five written names. (5) **What Vastin has told the six about the layer is four things only:** no key (it cannot be reached); the citation; the suppressed records; the technician's line. He has not defined "classification event" and does not know which event is meant. Nothing on the page says that menders, technicians or any office have tried to open it or know more. (6) **Speakers:** "What follows you," was Lira's; "She's right. Go and lie down, and don't take the stairs fast," was Oryn's. (7) **Deployment since the Line is thirty** at the end of Movement 2 (the Iron read at the landing on the 277th). Purse 118 marks. (8) **Teague's spear** has "he/his" on the page from chapter 7 (OWNER-pending #59 as defaulted). (9) Vastin has shown no Iron Wall, has no stated age, has asked only for a bed, and holds Karis's unsealed receipt. Cael has not touched the page and has not read the sheet's date closely.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:19:  - From `BOOK_MAP.md`: §2 items 27–31; §3 A, C (294th; road east); §5 (the Teague cutaway); §7.1 (Force; Rune; the still place); §10 Tier A 11, 16, 23, 25, 27 and the S17–S18 Tier C lines; §12 C2, C4; §13 (the "Noted" order; Vastin's order).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:24:It is the 294th day. The list of parts takes all day, and Cleon's finger is on the last line at the bell. Twelve fragments. Karis's hand is bound and she writes with it anyway. Vastin is on day 15 of a month. There is still no mule.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:28:The book turns east, on the same road read backwards. Two crews join by contract and not by friendship. Cael watches the Force line in a meadow and does not yet know where it will matter. The grade is cracked, and the sites run oldest-last into the deep edge. At Millrace the healer reads him as deep as she goes. Meanwhile, and against the card, the second instrument turns inward by itself. We are in the last third now: progression surfaces at turning points, and the grade's vocabulary is counted separately (§7.2).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:32:- **The road east (295th–297th; ~5,000).** On the bridge he counts five piers, and does not look at the crown. The spring, with the wind in their faces this time. The fork passed. The shoulder hold's factor: "He said you'd say that." **The cut revisited:** "Here." Vastin puts his weight on the knee with the stick off the ground, once. "Two words. Both of them ours." / "Noted" (Cael's). The feeling of being *known* is entered under each date.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:33:- **Lowmarch (297th).** Pike: *Treswick. Survey read. Bearing.* The price and outcome columns are left blank, and the season line is dated. Cael reads the line the right way up. **Teague's term and contract, verbatim:** ten on a wall's count; shares by count; the field is Teague's; the reading is Karis's. "Contract. Not more than that." / "The wall's still the wall." Cael prices it honestly: Teague is the better field captain, and the rival clock still runs.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:34:- **Force seen (298th morning).** The meadow cart. The frame lined up heel to palm, a body's length. The wrist clicks, and the young one's cloth is ready. "Don't put it in front of anything that needs doing twice." Cael enters the line and its cost.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:35:- **The grade cracked (298th morning).** Teague is at the door for the dividers, not the marks. There are three marks; the box for the first tier is ruled and never used. Cleon's list puts the kindling mark and the sheet mark in one line: "A mark is a grade." Ages by first sheet: 61, 94, 138, 206. The third-tier point falls past the fourth, in the straightedge's shadow. **Oldest-last.** "It's observation … Not what it means." **Vastin's first "Noted."** Teague: "Oldest last." / "Then that's where we're going." **The log, verbatim** (the grandmother is *Cael's*: §12 C4).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:36:- **Millrace (298th evening).** "Eleven off the ridge." / "I know." The healers exchange one look, then both look at Brom's shoulder. Vastin is ordered to stand ("Nineteen days." / "Then it's eleven more."); it is his first order taken without walking it back. Oryn restates her terms: three holds owed, and "a stop on my own route". "Sixth chair." / "On my terms. Which are the only kind." **She asks each patient, "May I?"** The readings: Brom's shoulder; Lira's arm ("You listened when it told you the second time." / "Once." / "Once is once more than I priced"); Karis's hand ("Who sewed this."); the knee ("It held in a cut"; "Noted" / "That's new." / "It's a useful word." / "It's his.").
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:37:- **The deep reading (~3,000).** "May I?" / "Yes." It is the long one. Her current goes round the place. **The twelfth turns inward unbidden: *still*, then *set*.** It is not named, and he keeps the check out of his wrist and the change out of his face. The eyes pay in the dark. **Oryn's finding, verbatim.** He withholds his own and enters his reasons in order. Lira offers the leaf. "Is it a finding?" / "It's a leaf …" / "Then it's not mine … Tell me on the road, if there's road. Not at my table."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:42:**Development:** about 14 Cael beats. Supporting: Karis 2, Oryn 2, Vastin 2, Teague 2, Lira 1, Brom 1, the young one 1, Pike 1.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:50:- "Noted" order: Vastin's first is here. Teague does not say it yet.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:55:How the road east reads in reverse. The plank room's crowd. The meadow's details. Teague's crew at the table. How the grade's numbers come off the sheets. Millrace's lean-to, light and noise. How long the deep reading takes on the page.
