editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:28:This is the archive's first week. Karis has found the room she has wanted all her life. A marshal learns his name is a blade with no handle. A craftsman shows how he reads a made thing's bones. Brom is offered the life his family wanted and picks up a box. Seln looks at the door his old trade would have used and decides nothing. Then the faction reaches inside the walls. A man with nothing behind him holds a line for people the Compact would restrict, and Cael comes away with the eleventh. We cross the first third into the middle, and progression language surfaces at the turning points: Rune explained, Iron Wall paid, the notice.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:31:- **The Deepstacks (284th).** The galleries, the shelving, the smell of a place where nothing has been decided. Cleon reads to the end of his page first. The sheets are laid out 11/29/12. Karis: "Older than [UNBOUND]." Cleon: "I know that hand." "Being believed … It's the end of being able to be wrong." "Give me a week." Cael finds himself, for the first time, unfiled.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:32:- **The yard door (285th).** Vastin's reflex: "Vastin. Archmarshal, Compact enforcement. You'll find the name is —". **Seln answers truthfully** (ruling 25): "He's on the count … the form asks what a hand's for, not what he was." The narration records that Seln did not lie and what not lying cost him. "I'm sorry." / "Don't be sorry. Be nobody." Cael's fellow-feeling on the landing. **The log, verbatim.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:33:- **The chamber days (285th–289th; ~8,000 on the page, including the 288th–289th the source left undramatized).**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:36:  - Cael wants the instrument turned on himself, notes the wish and does not say it.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:38:  - **Vastin learning to be nobody**, badly. He moves toward the lamp four times on the fourth day. "How long did it take you." / "I was fourteen. I'm nineteen. I'm not there yet either."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:39:- **Brom's yard (~2,000).** He rights a broker's cart with his back and no Path, spending the good shoulder. The broker offers a guard's post, a pass and a bed inside the second wall. "I'll think on it." He picks up the box on the bound shoulder, a debt Cael enters. On the stair: "You think Karis is right?" … "Good. I'd hate to have turned down a real job for a wrong hunch."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:40:- **Seln's night walk.** Cael hears the room change shape. From a roof below the walls Seln looks at the registry and the station's light. "I looked at it." It is six words in the morning log.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:41:- **Cleon's close (287th), verbatim:** "documentation … built the same way twice … never once slept well since."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:42:- **The alley (290th dusk; ~4,000, developed).** Staging follows BOOK_MAP §8. Vastin turns uphill and roots the cut wall to wall: "there is no round." Nobody declares. Brom with a loose step-stone. Lira's drop, the knife into the stave's shaft. Cael stands still at the plane's foot for a minute and some, as "the reason". Seln's weighted cord from the roof takes the signaller. The cache was on the roof the whole time. They leave: none taken, no faces, nobody dead.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:43:- **Costs and the acquisition.** Karis's left hand is cut on a step's edge. Brom binds it with thread, a strip of shirt and his teeth, because no healer inside the gate would put hands on it. Vastin is spent past the road and the knee goes again. **The Iron-Wall notice renders, verbatim.** "I put the wall in front of it anyway. I'd like that entered" / "It's entered." **Not told.** The faction's limit is entered as a finding. **The log, verbatim.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:45:**Physical challenge:** the alley (a major fight) and Brom's cart.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:47:**Development:** about 15 Cael beats. Supporting: Vastin 3, Brom 2, Seln 2, Karis 2, Cleon 2, Lira 1.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:52:- The eleventh is acquired in the alley's quiet middle minute, after Iron Wall has been witnessed in use: the cut first, then this full minute. It is **not deployed and not told** to Vastin.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:56:- Vastin does not know the mechanism and his age is not stated. "Forty years" is his rounding.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:60:The galleries' geography. The order of the chamber days, and which small discoveries Karis makes on which day. Brom's yard and the broker's words. How the alley's minute feels from two feet below a plane. Where the humour sits: the lamp, the chairs with and without cushions, Brom's "Cart was heavier".
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:64:The faction knows where they sleep, and they know the crew knows it. A man who held a wall for them has asked for it to be entered, and Cael has entered more than the man knows. Karis has three days left of Cleon's week. A board leans, and a boy holding a lamp has started to notice which way.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:10:> **[Coordinator rulings after the Movement 1 audit, 2026-10-11 — binding; they override any plan text below that differs.]** (1) **Teague's spear is a tall MAN** (he / him): the locked Book 7 wrote him so (ch25, ch51, ch52), and Book 8 follows its own edition (OWNER-pending #59). Where the plan says "the tall woman", read "the tall man"; his silence toward the six until his question at the pass stands. (2) **Teague can read** (locked Book 7 ch25: he read a slip twice). Never write that he cannot; if he does not read a sheet it is because it is not in front of him or he has no need. (3) **Lira's asking:** she asked Oryn once about the ankle on the mountain in Book 7 and asked nobody for anything from then until Thornwater; do not call Thornwater her first ask since Norhold. (4) **The stroke and bar** is on stake thirty-two (the Stair's newer stake and the kit's unused one) and on the fourth site's thirty-four ONLY; stakes thirty-one and thirty-three do not carry it. Later records may show the grade on survey SHEETS; the field stakes do not all carry it. (5) **The cord:** the kit's cord is twenty strides, knotted at the fives (four knots to a length); Book 7's Ring was sixty-two cords and twenty strides round. The court is about 1,107 yards across, which is about FIFTY cords, not 159. Give no yardage for a cord. (6) **"West"** was first said aloud at the six-person table on the 268th (Karis's protected "It's west… Treswick…" speech, printed once in ch6). (7) **Deployment since the Line is twenty-nine** at the end of Movement 1 (two uses of the Iron read in earnest); trials are not counted.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:12:> **[Coordinator rulings after the Movement 2 audit, 2026-10-11 — binding; they override any plan text below that differs.]** (1) **Vastin's second paper is "the page": a COPY in his own hand** of one line from an old register ("—of the Architect: see the lower archive at Treswick, which holds it in full—"). It was never cut from anything and is never called a leaf; "the leaf" is the chamber record of Movement 6 only. (2) **The technician's sheet carries a Compact date (a registry year and a day in it) that is NEVER printed as figures** anywhere in this book; whoever reads it reads a date, and the page does not give its numbers. The office filed that sheet at the end of the second row of the records, and it lies there. (3) **The anomaly column:** on every survey abstract, in every hand, for six years, the entry is the one word *Total* — an entry, not a sum. (4) **The Fallow completion report** carries five strokes for a name and a count of six (locked Book 7), not five written names. (5) **What Vastin has told the six about the layer is four things only:** no key (it cannot be reached); the citation; the suppressed records; the technician's line. He has not defined "classification event" and does not know which event is meant. Nothing on the page says that menders, technicians or any office have tried to open it or know more. (6) **Speakers:** "What follows you," was Lira's; "She's right. Go and lie down, and don't take the stairs fast," was Oryn's. (7) **Deployment since the Line is thirty** at the end of Movement 2 (the Iron read at the landing on the 277th). Purse 118 marks. (8) **Teague's spear** has "he/his" on the page from chapter 7 (OWNER-pending #59 as defaulted). (9) Vastin has shown no Iron Wall, has no stated age, has asked only for a bed, and holds Karis's unsealed receipt. Cael has not touched the page and has not read the sheet's date closely.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:19:  - From `BOOK_MAP.md`: §2 items 15–18; §3 B 1, C (Treswick); §4 (the quiet-movement statement); §5 (the Oryn and Vastin cutaways); §7.1 (Tide, the still place); §10 (S7–S9 lines; Tier A 24); §12 C2, C9; §13.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:24:It is the 281st day, on the border road's last stretch. The city grows by the wayposts: nine miles, six, three. There are six of them and no mule. The boxes are on Brom's good shoulder, on Lira and on Cael, and the kit's case is on Vastin, who picked it up at the fork-stone unasked. Vastin has walked beside Cael since the rise.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:28:This is the book's one partly quiet movement. The reason: its tension is legal and bodily, a [SHATTERED] body entering a Compact city whose top holds a station. It does not need a fight. It holds a learning encounter in which an instrument fails, a confession, the city shown as a machine, and the irony that the only legal door into the oldest record of what Cael is admits him as a number. Progression teaching stays dense in the first third: the ten as currents, the Path-tiered city (passes, tier gates, the smith's two forges), and the provision's columns.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:31:- **The reading inward (281st, the six-mile post).** First he works out the line between "stop touching it" and "do not read yourself". Then come the fourth and fifth readings. The ten are named as currents. The still place is read *around*, not touched. **Finding: the reading feels current; the still place has none; "a cord on a stone."** He needs an instrument for what does not move. He writes down later that he is afraid of that.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:32:- **Cael and Vastin on the road's edge.** Vastin sits, for the first time since the cut. "I read your file …" (the span anchored, not numbered: §12 C2). "You were the instrument." / "I was the error." **The confession, as narrowed:** "I declined to read you a second time. You know that. What you do not know is why." In return Cael gives him the instrument's nothing, the thing nobody else holds. It is not friendship. It is ground. Then **the log, verbatim** ("color" stands).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:33:- **Treswick (282nd).** The grey bridge is older than the walls. The outer gate counts heads and asks for nothing. The outer district works as a mechanism. The mule at the trough. The inn with two doors: 136. Each of them looks at the city in their own way. Vastin: "I have papers I will not show. I want that said once." Brom: "They shoe by the tier." Cael walks the district's edge. **The road to the registry crosses the square**, and the promise holds. **Seln's report:** the quarry, the provision, hands entered by count, the clerk, the exposure. "Four hands." / "I've two." "Entered by count. That's the door." **The close, verbatim.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:35:- **The provision (284th).** They go up by count under Cleon's pass, which the keepers count with a pen. The square is avoided by Seln's route. Four hands: Cael, Brom, Lira and Vastin, who says "Yes" before anyone can ask. Seln is not on the count. The clerk does not ask, and writes "four". **Lira's ladder does not pull.** The iron door. "The tiers closed, and the dark opened."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:38:**Cutaways (~4,000):** Oryn, ~2,500, on her north circuit: Oxhollow's gate, a man with a wrist set wrong, a birth, the unread ribs on her mind. Vastin, ~1,500, in the outer district inn ("the first honest district"). He knows nothing of the mechanism and does no date arithmetic.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:39:**Development:** about 15 Cael beats. Supporting: Vastin 2–3, Lira 2, Seln 1–2, Karis 1–2, Brom 1, Oryn 2, Cleon 1.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:43:- Cael never sets foot on the square or the station steps, and does not look at the crown. Lira keeps the same discipline unasked.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:44:- Lira's paper is **registry paper, Iron first rank, formal** (§12 C9), and stays unshown.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:45:- Cleon's Path and tier come through Seln's report ("Rune Path. Bronze.": ruling 17). Cleon takes no notice of Cael. Cleon's Path is **not shown** in this movement. Bones come in Movement 5.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:46:- No fragment is acquired here. The still place is not touched or turned on, and the twelfth does not yet exist.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:48:- Vastin's age is not stated. The clerk is not named and asks nothing.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:52:Treswick's texture: brokers' tally boards, the rope-walk, the ferry landing, the smith's two forges and the coloured coats at the gates. Which way Cael walks the district's edge. Whether the optional physical beat happens and what it is. How the counter talk about strata goes, heard through the yard door.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:56:Cael is through an iron door older than the walls, as a hand carrying a box, into a dark that had been there before any of it was. Above him a whole city reads bodies. Below him nothing reads anything. He has a question he has never let anyone hold, and he is about to watch a stranger whose craft is reading how things are built.

