editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-007/pre-repair/chapter-52.md:73:She had said at the stone that she would not sit outside a second day and listen. Four people were holding the rim who knew what a crossbow was; and she had found out what it was worth to be on the right side of a line when the line was shut. She meant to be where a certain shoulder was; and if anything opened, it could be carried up forty steps and two hundred yards with her walking beside it.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-007/pre-repair/chapter-52.md:331:He had been over the floor, and through the grass below the stone, and he had an armful of ash shafts, which he laid on the turf in a row beside four crossbows, one of which was in two pieces.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-007/pre-repair/chapter-51.md:19:He had priced this on the stair. There was one bolt in that groove, and when it was gone, a boot must go into a stirrup and a hook onto a string, and a back must straighten; he had watched that man do it once, from a frozen road, and it had taken him something over twenty counts. One bolt, then, and after it twenty counts in which a bow was a stick. He had been told on a bluff never to spend the Wind near a thing whose single blow he could not price. He could price this one to a hair.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-007/pre-repair/chapter-51.md:181:When he came down he had a crossbow in his hands.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-007/pre-repair/chapter-51.md:189:Cael had known him for two years. He had seen him carve a goat, and wax a seal, and stand in a doorway with his back to a room, and he had never seen him do a thing in anger. Seln lifted the crossbow over his head and brought it down across the grey stone with the whole of his narrow strength, and the stock broke in two at the lock. He stood over it, breathing.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-007/pre-repair/chapter-51.md:237:He was of the middle height, and heavy in the forearm, and there was a band of black leather laced on his right wrist. He stopped at the edge of their lamplight, and Cael saw his eyes go round it once, slowly. They went to a big man lying on his left side under a healer's coat, and to a girl whose sling was tied a hand higher than it had been at a certain door. They went to two pieces of a crossbow lying side by side by a grey stone. They came to Cael, and to his hands.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-007/pre-repair/chapter-51.md:353:That was a crossbow. He had expected a bow of some kind. He had not expected that every sign of its owner would stop at the height of a boot.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-007/pre-repair/chapter-51.md:359:He sent the spear south-about by the ruts with the lantern, and the boy with him. They were gone the better part of two hours. They came back by the north, having walked the whole of the ruts, with a crossbow each and a third across the boy's shoulders.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-003/review-editorial-prompt.md:1629:On top of the pack, lashed along it in an oiled cover, there was something with the shape of a crossbow.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-003/review-editorial-prompt.md:1909:Oryn had loaded the mule in the hollow. Two of the boxes hung from the pack-saddle, one on either flank, and her own panniers were lashed on top with the crossbow in its cover. She took the animal by the cheek-strap and walked it to the edge of the break, and there she changed her hand and put herself on the outside.
