    55	- The Iron Wall shown here is Vastin's. **Cael does not acquire it here.** The eleventh comes in the alley (Movement 5).
    56	- The deep-layer arithmetic is Cael's and Seln's alone. It is never spoken or written, and **never interpreted**.
    57	- Karis never finishes the lamps sentence. The grade stays unread. There is no claim about who graded the sites or why.
    58	- Vastin's age is not stated. Oryn does not read Cael; "the one thing I'm walking up that road owing".
    59	- The fork is on this side of the long rise. Oryn's condition was first written "at the fork above Millrace" in Book 7.
    60	- Reader Standard: the hounds die without gore. Oryn binds the knee and gets two fingers on the wrist, after she asks and receives an explicit yes; the form never substitutes for consent [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 21].
    61	
    62	## What the author owns
    63	
    64	The drill's details and Vastin's mistakes in it. Exactly how the pack moves on ice. How long the scouting takes. The spring's light and wind. The order in which the three readers find things. How Oryn prices each of them, and the fork's last fire. Whether Vastin's three reflexes come in one scene or across the halt.
    65	
    66	## Where we leave pressure
    67	
    68	A city stands on a bluff ahead, with three walls in tiers and a light on its crown. A healer's term is written in the log. A man on a stick has learned one sentence from a defector, and a boy carries a date he will not write down. Five people and a marshal walk toward the first registry Cael has ever gone to on purpose.
