+# PLAN / CANON / PROTECTED-TEXT AUDIT — Movement 3
+
+## VERDICT: REPAIR
+
+Repair chapters 13–19 locally before closure. The movement's calendar, entry seam, bodies, money, names, Reader Standard, and principal beat order are sound, but it cannot be ratified with only marker substitution. Required repair scope is: restore seven incomplete protected units (the slip plus six markers); remove the unplanned Ember deployment and close at deployment **thirty-one**; restore the map-locked cut positions and sequence; keep the protected log's irreducible “two feet from me” wording without rewriting it; withhold the fifth site and its different grade until the later reveal; remove the invented stations-calendar conversion and Vastin's participation in the date arithmetic; correct the field-stake distribution; narrow the surveyor-hand claim and the gloss on “Behaves as device”; restore Oryn's source event; hand Movement 4 the three boxes and kit case in its packet-locked custody; and cut Cael's unplanned first touch of the copied page. The exact replacements are below.
+
+## 1. Continuity with the closed text
+
+### Ratified continuity
+
+- The entry is correctly the morning of day 278 at Lowmarch (`manuscript/chapter-13.md:21`), immediately after the CLOSED Movement 2 night on day 277 (`STATE_LEDGER.md:250,292`). The purse opens at 118 (`manuscript/chapter-13.md:163,265`; `STATE_LEDGER.md:272`), deployment at thirty (`manuscript/chapter-13.md:269`; `STATE_LEDGER.md:254`), and Cael still has ten fragments and has not touched the copied page (`manuscript/chapter-13.md:3–17`; `STATE_LEDGER.md:254`).
+- Paper custody crosses the seam correctly: Karis folds the copied page in its oilcloth and packs the records flat (`manuscript/chapter-13.md:3–17`), preserving her custody of the flat, six rows, completion report, original technician's sheet at the end of row two, copied page, and her copy (`STATE_LEDGER.md:260,272,285`). Vastin remains off the sheet and follows at the back (`manuscript/chapter-13.md:39,109–113,171–175`), matching the CLOSED entry (`STATE_LEDGER.md:266,287`).
+- Bodies and carried objects hold at entry: Lira's left arm is slow (`manuscript/chapter-13.md:77–79,169`), Brom's right shoulder stays in the older healer's knot (`manuscript/chapter-13.md:63`; `manuscript/chapter-16.md:133`), the three boxes remain roped on the mule (`manuscript/chapter-13.md:103–105`), and Seln's case stays shut (`manuscript/chapter-18.md:39–41`; `packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:20–23,50`).
+- Ferry and rope continuity is exact: the ferry takes people, carried sacks and the mule but no wheels (`manuscript/chapter-13.md:115–145`); the western-bank stock is three-strand and Brom refuses it, leaving sixty yards of four-strand owed (`manuscript/chapter-13.md:149–165`; `STATE_LEDGER.md:272`; `packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:22`). Seven crew coppers are spent and Vastin pays his own (`manuscript/chapter-13.md:137–145`); no whole mark leaves the 118-mark purse.
+- Teague's forty sacks are on the east landing on day 278 and his cold-road departure remains prospective (`manuscript/chapter-13.md:115–135`), which legitimately resolves the open Movement 2 location without naming a crew member (`packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:22`). The tall spear-carrier has he/his (`manuscript/chapter-13.md:115,135`), as OWNER #59 requires (`OWNER-DECISIONS.md:182–188`).
+- The crossbow transfer is continuous: Lira carries Oryn's crossbow and one bolt into the cut (`manuscript/chapter-13.md:169`; `manuscript/chapter-14.md:191–195`), then returns it to Oryn, and it goes north on Oryn's mule (`manuscript/chapter-19.md:207,217–219`). Locked Book 7 left the bow and one bolt with Lira (`book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-58.md:23`; `STATE_LEDGER.md:14,64`).
+- The fight's body ledger is correct: eight hounds (`manuscript/chapter-14.md:243–245`), five dead and three through the sink (`manuscript/chapter-15.md:179–197`), Brom's right boot/two toes/ten days (`manuscript/chapter-16.md:75,187`), and Vastin's right knee shut and bound for a month after “May I?” / “Yes” (`manuscript/chapter-16.md:27–65,187`). The bad knee had no side in Movement 2 (`STATE_LEDGER.md:239,266`), so “right” is compatible rather than contradictory.
+- The purse closes correctly at 138: 118 at departure plus the hold's twenty (`manuscript/chapter-16.md:99–101,187`; `packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:35,44`). Brom holds Pike's thumbed slip with the purse (`manuscript/chapter-16.md:99–101`). The reserve is never opened.
+
+### Continuity repairs
+
+- **Deployment:** the draft adds an Ember grain (`manuscript/chapter-14.md:167–181,233–235`; `manuscript/chapter-16.md:205`) and therefore reports thirty-two (`manuscript/chapter-16.md:211`). The packet gives the cut one Cael use in earnest—Wind away—and locks the eleventh to Movement 5 (`packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:44,55`; `BOOK_MAP.md:260`; `packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:42–43,52`). Cut Ember and close at **thirty-one**. No later packet fixes a conflicting numeric count; the repair follows the present movement's exclusive beat and preserves the sequence lock.
+- **Movement 4 load seam:** the present close puts the second box on Seln and the tarred kit case on Lira (`manuscript/chapter-19.md:193,207,253,295`). The next packet opens with boxes on Brom, Lira and Cael and the kit case on Vastin, picked up at the fork-stone unasked (`packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:24`). Repair custody before closure.
+- **Copied page:** Cael's first touch on the rise is invented (`manuscript/chapter-19.md:271–291`). Neither Movement 3 nor any later packet places a first touch there; Movement 4 instead makes the next pressure the inward reading and explicitly keeps the still place untouched (`packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:31,43,46`). Preserve Karis's custody and Cael's non-touch.
+
+## 2. The movement plan and every Owner flag
+
+### Beat order and withheld truths
+
+The order is otherwise correct: slip and road drill on 278 (`manuscript/chapter-13.md:21–269`); scouting and cut on 279 (`manuscript/chapter-14.md:1–249`; `manuscript/chapter-15.md:1–229`); costs, lesson and log on the 279th evening (`manuscript/chapter-16.md:1–213`); three-reader spring and Seln cutaway on 280 (`manuscript/chapter-17.md:1–241`; `manuscript/chapter-18.md:1–249`); fork on the 280th evening and Treswick from the rise on the 281st (`manuscript/chapter-19.md:3–295`). This matches the packet (`packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:35–47`) and calendar spine (`BOOK_MAP.md:203–223`).
+
+With repairs below, the withheld facts stay withheld: Cael does not acquire Iron Wall (`manuscript/chapter-15.md:223–227`; `packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:55`); the sequence is not interpreted (`manuscript/chapter-18.md:119–127`; `packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:56`); Karis does not finish the lamps sentence (`manuscript/chapter-17.md:93–103`; `packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:45,57`); the grade remains unread and nobody says who assigned it or why (`manuscript/chapter-17.md:161–181`; `packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:57`); Seln's case stays shut (`manuscript/chapter-18.md:39–41`; `packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:50`); Oryn does not read Cael (`manuscript/chapter-19.md:171–185`; `packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:58`); and Vastin never learns what Cael carries (`manuscript/chapter-15.md:223–227`; `STATE_LEDGER.md:266`).
+
+### Owner flags 1–16
+
+1. **Six markers — REPAIR.** All six are partial or missing, not publishable protected units (`AUTHOR-REPORT.md:135`; `manuscript/chapter-16.md:93,165`; `manuscript/chapter-17.md:185`; `manuscript/chapter-18.md:219`; `manuscript/chapter-19.md:177,215`). Fixes 41, 43, 67, 79, 88 and 93 restore them.
+2. **Lesson speakers — KEEP.** Vastin owns “The wall held the line…” and “I know fields…”; Cael owns “You do now” (`manuscript/chapter-16.md:159–169`; source `chapter-04.md:165–169`; `BOOK_MAP.md:394`).
+3. **Cut staging — REPAIR.** “Twenty strides west” is Cael's station past the sink, not an Ember bait mark; the wall is two feet behind Brom, and the pack turns to the wall because it is loud (`BOOK_MAP.md:323`; source `chapter-04.md:57–89`). The draft instead makes twenty strides the mark, walks Cael back beside Brom, raises the wall two feet from Cael, and makes the den run to where a declaration ends (`manuscript/chapter-14.md:167–181,223–249`; `manuscript/chapter-15.md:3–35`; `manuscript/chapter-16.md:117,189`). Fixes 2–40 restore the planned geometry and sequence. The protected log still says “two feet from me” (`manuscript/chapter-16.md:197`; `BOOK_MAP.md:394`); that source/map conflict is irreducible without altering protected text, so the log stays verbatim and unglossed.
+4. **“The fourth's twice the size” — KEEP.** It is the **place** whose measure is double, while the stroke and bar are the same size (`manuscript/chapter-17.md:163–173`; source `chapter-05.md:57–65`; `packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:45`).
+5. **“Five” / fifth site — CUT.** The packet gives only the four known sites and holds the fifth-site structure for the later age/grade reveal (`packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:45,57`; `BOOK_MAP.md:36,82`). The draft prematurely creates a fifth place, its larger measure and a different class box (`manuscript/chapter-17.md:27–41,59,113,177–187`; `manuscript/chapter-18.md:161`; `manuscript/chapter-19.md:239`). Fixes 46–51, 58, 65–66, 78 and 95 preserve “more than four” as unread sign groups while limiting findings to the four sites on the hide.
+6. **Two calendar counts — CUT.** A separate stations year and a spoken offset are invented, implicate Vastin in the sum, and collide with the ruling that the sheet already bears a Compact date (`manuscript/chapter-17.md:127–133`; `manuscript/chapter-18.md:9–27,59,99–107`; `packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:12,45,56`; `OWNER-DECISIONS.md:190–191`). Fixes 59–61 and 69–76 keep the unprinted arithmetic exclusively with Seln and Cael without minting calendar machinery or a span.
+7. **Dead surveyor's hand — AMEND.** The sheet is properly a Stair abstract in the fourth yearly row (`manuscript/chapter-17.md:77–85`; `STATE_LEDGER.md:242`), but the source establishes only that the hand is dead by the sheet's date, not that it is the kit surveyor's hand (`books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-05.md:33–37`). Fixes 52 and 57 remove the overclaim and the later causal join.
+8. **Oryn's past — AMEND.** Book 7 does not contradict a city past, but the retained source event is a year healing inside walls, Bronze-and-above first, and the yard going septic—not a forty-bed house, six healers, a fever week and a secretly saved untiered woman (`manuscript/chapter-19.md:33–53`; source `chapter-06.md:25`; `BOOK_MAP.md:66`). Fixes 80–87 restore the event while retaining her provisional Iron fourth rank and the patient's-tier column.
+9. **Crossbow north with Oryn — KEEP** (`manuscript/chapter-14.md:191–195`; `manuscript/chapter-19.md:207–219`; locked Book 7 `chapter-58.md:23`).
+10. **Rope refused; 118 → 138 — KEEP** (`manuscript/chapter-13.md:149–165`; `manuscript/chapter-16.md:99–101`; `STATE_LEDGER.md:272`).
+11. **Factor has no pronoun — KEEP.** The factor is unnamed and ungendered throughout (`manuscript/chapter-14.md:59–105`; `packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:8`).
+12. **Vastin's right knee / no tier / eleven fields — KEEP.** Movement 2 gave no side, so right is compatible; no tier appears; “eleven” is a career incident count, not a forbidden age or ability ceiling (`manuscript/chapter-16.md:27–65,107,145`; `STATE_LEDGER.md:239,266`).
+13. **Cael touches the page — CUT** for the reasons in §1 (`manuscript/chapter-19.md:271–291`; `packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:31,46`). Fixes 97–102.
+14. **Cutaway length — KEEP.** 2,131 words against “about 1,800” is a 331-word development variance, not a canon fault (`AUTHOR-REPORT.md:24,148`; `packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:50`).
+15. **Chapter 10 frame shop — RESOLVED / no action.** No frame-shop or mender claim survives in this movement (`AUTHOR-REPORT.md:149`; `manuscript/chapter-13.md:1–269` through `chapter-19.md:1–295`).
+16. **Probe arguments — NOT A TEXT FLAG.** The reported movement invocation is the applicable one (`AUTHOR-REPORT.md:36,150`). Section 7 rules on the result.
+
+## 3. Calendar
+
+- Day 278 is Lowmarch, ferry and road day one (`manuscript/chapter-13.md:21,103–175,259–269`); day 279 is the shoulder hold and cut (`manuscript/chapter-14.md:3`; `manuscript/chapter-16.md:187`); day 280 is the spring and fork evening (`manuscript/chapter-16.md:235`; `manuscript/chapter-19.md:5`); day 281 is first light and the rise (`manuscript/chapter-19.md:191,233–261`). This exactly matches `packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:43–47` and `BOOK_MAP.md:203–223`.
+- “Two days west” works: the crew leaves Lowmarch on 278 and reaches the cut on 279 (`manuscript/chapter-13.md:27,103–175`; `manuscript/chapter-14.md:3`). The spring is reached on 280 and the fork that evening (`manuscript/chapter-16.md:235–271`; `manuscript/chapter-19.md:3–15`). Treswick is first visible from the rise before noon on 281, a day's walk away, and Cael does not look at the pale steady crown light (`manuscript/chapter-19.md:233–263`).
+- No printed figure appears for the Compact date and no numeric span since Kindling is computed (`manuscript/chapter-18.md:95–139`; `OWNER-DECISIONS.md:190–191`). The draft's alternate-calendar offset is nevertheless unauthorized machinery and is removed by fixes 59–61 and 69–76.
+
+## 4. Standing defaults and progression accounting
+
+- **Pass:** no English month or weekday name; no named season; “cold term,” “thaw,” generic “season,” and the water **spring** are permitted weather/period/place words (`manuscript/chapter-13.md:99,107,149`; `manuscript/chapter-16.md:235`; `OWNER-DECISIONS.md:148–150`). No metric unit occurs in the edition draft; measures are feet, yards, paces, strides and furlongs (`manuscript/chapter-14.md:111–127`; `manuscript/chapter-19.md:225–251`).
+- **Pass:** Cael is nineteen and has no birthday here (`manuscript/chapter-13.md:175`; `manuscript/chapter-19.md:295`; `BOOK_MAP.md:22`). No narration says “his Path” or assigns Cael a Path; the ten remain fragments (`manuscript/chapter-15.md:221–227`; `OWNER-DECISIONS.md:154–157`).
+- **Pass:** Reader Standard. The hounds die by impact, knife or water without gore (`manuscript/chapter-15.md:67–81,115–123,159–197`). The only blood is a restrained injury cue at Vastin's trouser leg (`manuscript/chapter-15.md:127`), followed by consent and clinical binding (`manuscript/chapter-16.md:27–65`).
+- **Progression after repair:** Wind is the sole use in earnest, taking deployment 30 → **31** (`manuscript/chapter-15.md:133–163`; `packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:44`). Shadow rises and is held, never opened (`manuscript/chapter-13.md:259`; `manuscript/chapter-16.md:127`); Anchor is refused and stays at two counted uses (`manuscript/chapter-14.md:221`; `STATE_LEDGER.md:254`); Tide is not used, no self-read occurs, and Oryn does not read Cael (`manuscript/chapter-16.md:47`; `manuscript/chapter-19.md:171–185`). Ten fragments remain at movement end; the eleventh is reserved for Movement 5 (`manuscript/chapter-15.md:223–227`; `packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:52`).
+- **Iron Wall:** the mechanics are correct once the positions are repaired: a plane wall-to-wall, rooted at Vastin's feet, immobile, loud, reserve-draining, and unable to seal the banks (`manuscript/chapter-15.md:23–67`; `BOOK_MAP.md:260,323`). No earlier Monroe 1.3 Books 1–7 manuscript shows Iron Wall on page; Movement 2 explicitly closed with none shown (`STATE_LEDGER.md:239,266,292`). At the cut Vastin sees the crew's silent doctrine used around his rooted field habit (`manuscript/chapter-16.md:137–179`); at the spring he sees that his directive/classification/escalation reflexes identify him and receives Seln's first lesson (`manuscript/chapter-17.md:125–157`; `manuscript/chapter-18.md:159–205`). He is never framed as joining and never learns Cael's mechanism (`manuscript/chapter-13.md:109–113`; `manuscript/chapter-19.md:235–269`; `STATE_LEDGER.md:266`).
