+54. `manuscript/chapter-17.md`
+   old: `"He does not say. I suppose that nobody could tell him who had made such a thing, or how it would be made; and a surveyor is not paid to suppose." She had taken her hand away. "I felt it, at three of those lines. So did four of you. There was no dimming. It went out at one stride, for a third rank and a first and a Copper alike, and came back at the same stride, whole. It was not as a person tires. It was as a row of lamps—"`
+   new: `"He does not say." She had taken her hand away. "I felt it, at three of those lines. So did four of you. There was no dimming. It went out at one stride, for a third rank and a first and a Copper alike, and came back at the same stride, whole. It was not as a person tires. It was as a row of lamps—"`
