57:- No printed figure appears for the Compact date and no numeric span since Kindling is computed (`manuscript/chapter-18.md:95–139`; `OWNER-DECISIONS.md:190–191`). The draft's alternate-calendar offset is nevertheless unauthorized machinery and is removed by fixes 59–61 and 69–76.
75:- “Behaves as device. Cannot be.” is exact and once (`manuscript/chapter-17.md:85`; source `chapter-05.md:37`; `BOOK_MAP.md:354`). It is Karis reading a dead-by-date surveyor's remark from the Stair abstract in the fourth yearly row (`manuscript/chapter-17.md:77–85`); the present prose over-identifies the hand and over-glosses the words, repaired in fixes 52–56.
82:- The slip is partial (`manuscript/chapter-13.md:27` versus source `chapter-04.md:5`): restore the full protected unit, including the stillhound/sink, three carters, payment, witness and Brom's second reading (fix 1).
83:- The “clear” marker is only the tail of Seln's full unit (`manuscript/chapter-16.md:93`; source `chapter-04.md:147`): fix 41.
84:- “You do now” is missing Cael's tag (`manuscript/chapter-16.md:165`; source `chapter-04.md:167`): fix 43.
85:- “Two copies of one ignorance” belongs to Karis (`manuscript/chapter-17.md:185`; source `chapter-05.md:65`): fix 67.
