+   new: `It was a hundred strides long, as they had been told, and it fell from his left hand to his right, from east to west, by perhaps the height of two men in its whole length. The road in the bottom of it was no wider than a cart and a man walking beside. On the near side, the south, the bank was this same scree that he lay at the head of, loose plates of the dark stone lying at the pitch of a steep roof. The north bank was low. A man could have stepped up onto it; and beyond it the ground fell away again, steeply, down more of the same broken stone, to a hollow.`
