+92. `manuscript/chapter-19.md`
+   old: `"It's seven," said Brom. "I'll lay hers. Somebody can carry it empty for three weeks, and I'd as soon that it were me."`
+   new: `"It's seven," said Brom. "I'll lay hers. Somebody can carry it empty for three weeks, and I'd as soon that it were me."\n\nWhen the northern rut had taken Oryn and the mule out of sight, Vastin went back to the fork-stone. He picked up the tarred kit case by its strap without asking anybody and came after the other five.`
+
+93. `manuscript/chapter-19.md`
+   old: `He had a good deal to carry besides the box, and he went over it, a stride at a time, as he would have gone over a count. There was a job, done and paid, with a hundred and thirty-eight marks to show for it. There was a wall that he had stood behind for the space of one count, and an eleventh thing that had not come of it. There was a mark in a small ruled square, which was on five sheets and an iron stake and which nobody could read. He had a name, short and strange, for a man who sat under a town. He had two sentences in a book, in his own hand, about a flight of steps and a paved place.`
+   new: `He had a good deal to carry besides the box, and he went over it, a stride at a time, as he would have gone over a count. There was a job, done and paid, with a hundred and thirty-eight marks to show for it. There was a wall that he had stood behind for the space of one count, and an eleventh thing that had not come of it. There was a mark in a small ruled square, the same on four sites' sheets and on two iron stakes, which nobody could read. He had a name, short and strange, for a man who sat under a town. He had two sentences in a book, in his own hand, about a flight of steps and a paved place.`
+
+94. `manuscript/chapter-19.md`
+   old: `"Three tiers," said Lira, at his shoulder. She had set the tarred case down. "They've built the ladder out of stone. I'd wondered what it would look like from outside."`
+   new: `"Three tiers," said Lira, at his shoulder. She had set her box down. "They've built the ladder out of stone. I'd wondered what it would look like from outside."`
