+
+The field-stake correction is mandatory: the mark is on stake thirty-two and stake thirty-four only, while all four sites' **sheets** carry it (`manuscript/chapter-17.md:167–169`; `packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:10`). Fixes 61–62.
+
+## 7. Names, Reader Standard, and source-distance probe
+
+- No unapproved person, place or animal name is minted. Existing names are Cael, Lira, Brom, Karis, Seln, Oryn, Vastin, Pike, Teague, Hesk, Ostrand, Denvash, Lowmarch, Millrace and Treswick; Cleon is plan-required at the spring close (`manuscript/chapter-18.md:219–225`; `BOOK_MAP.md:395`). The shoulder factor, hold woman, broker, clerk, mule and Oryn's remembered city remain unnamed (`manuscript/chapter-14.md:59–105`; `manuscript/chapter-19.md:33–53`; `packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:8`).
+- The movement meets Reader Standard after the factual repairs: syntax and causal explanations are accessible; injury description is restrained; the fight's objective, positions, changed decision and cost are legible (`manuscript/chapter-14.md:109–249`; `manuscript/chapter-15.md:1–229`).
+- Sweep probe **2% skeleton / 15% close** is not by itself a copying finding (`AUTHOR-REPORT.md:36`). Fewer than roughly two percent of the 33,942 words are fixed protected/plan quotations; the higher close score in chapters 18–19 tracks required spring/fork dialogue plus Cael/Seln's recurring catalogue-and-count narration (`AUTHOR-REPORT.md:20,35–36`; `manuscript/chapter-18.md:1–225`; `manuscript/chapter-19.md:1–219`). The six literal markers account for about 150 non-prose words in the author's metric and disappear when fixed (`AUTHOR-REPORT.md:22,62–69`).
+
+## 8. Next-movement inheritance not already carried by Movement 4's packet
+
+Movement 4 already carries day 281, six people/no mule, boxes on Brom/Lira/Cael, kit case on Vastin, the road posts, the inward reads, the station promise, and no new fragment (`packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:24,31–33,43–46`). Its author must additionally inherit the following surviving details:
+
+- **Paper custody:** Karis has the flat under one arm and the hide under the other; inside the flat are six counted/re-taped rows with the original technician's sheet restored to the end of row two, plus the completion report and her copy; Vastin's copied page remains in its oilcloth inside her coat and Cael has still not touched it (`manuscript/chapter-18.md:141–149,155–157`; `manuscript/chapter-19.md:207,271–291` after fixes 95–101). Karis also has the dead surveyor's ledger/notebook; Seln's case remains shut on his own strap (`manuscript/chapter-17.md:183–187`; `manuscript/chapter-18.md:39–41`).
+- **Knowledge:** Cael and Seln alone know that the unprinted date matches Cael's Kindling day; neither has said or written it, neither has interpreted the sequence, and neither knows for certain what the other concluded (`manuscript/chapter-18.md:3–31,59–65,85–149`). Karis knows both men have read the sheet but not what they made of it (`manuscript/chapter-18.md:143–149`). Vastin heard the records reading but does not know the arithmetic, integration mechanism or Cael's fragments (`manuscript/chapter-18.md:159–205`; `STATE_LEDGER.md:266`). Oryn heard the archive discussion from the basin but not the date conclusion (`manuscript/chapter-18.md:229–231`; `packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:56`).
+- **Bodies:** Vastin's right knee is shut, lath-bound and on day two of Oryn's thirty-day month on the 281st; stick, no kneeling, no running, no wall, and he has finally accepted being priced equally (`manuscript/chapter-16.md:27–65`; `manuscript/chapter-19.md:151–169`). Brom's right two toes are bound with eight days left on the ten-day term, and his right shoulder remains in the older healer's knot; he must put a load down if it speaks (`manuscript/chapter-16.md:75`; `manuscript/chapter-19.md:131–139`). Lira's arm remains slow and is on day sixteen out of wool (`manuscript/chapter-19.md:119–129`).
+- **Oryn:** she and the brown mule are north of the fork on the reverse circuit; she has her linen and crossbow with one bolt. Her stated route is five gates, the ford and Millrace, where she expects the six in three weeks; she still owes Cael the proper reading and expects “all of it” from the archive (`manuscript/chapter-19.md:63–81,171–219`).
+- **Money/objects:** purse 138; reserve sealed; sixty yards of four-strand still owed; Pike's thumbed slip is in Brom's shirt; no cordage was bought (`manuscript/chapter-13.md:149–165`; `manuscript/chapter-16.md:99–101,187`). Oryn's empty bowl is Brom's to carry (`manuscript/chapter-19.md:221–223`).
+- **Progression:** ten fragments, deployment thirty-one after the sole Wind burst; Shadow sealed, Anchor still two, Tide unused, no self-read, no eleventh (`manuscript/chapter-15.md:133–163,223–227`; `manuscript/chapter-16.md:205–211` after fixes 44–45). Vastin has shown Iron Wall once; Cael witnessed it but did not acquire it (`packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:55`; `packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:52`).
+- **Treswick/day:** it is a little before noon on day 281, at the top of the long rise, a day's walk from Treswick. The six have seen a bluff, river loops, three tiered walls and the pale steady station light; Cael turned his eyes to the lowest wall, and Lira has not yet performed the packet's unasked matching discipline (`manuscript/chapter-19.md:233–269`; `packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:24,43`).
