+46. `manuscript/chapter-17.md`
+   old: `"Five," she said. "I said more than four, by a lamp, and that I should give a number when I had checked it in daylight. It is five. It is the same five in every one of six years; I cannot read a sign of them, and I can tell one group from another as I can tell your five faces."`
+   new: `"More than four," she said. "I said that much by a lamp, and daylight has not made the signs readable. The same groups recur in every one of six years; I can tell one group from another, and I shall not call each group a place until the paper lets me."`
