+## 7. Names, Reader Standard, and source-distance probe
+
+- No unapproved person, place or animal name is minted. Existing names are Cael, Lira, Brom, Karis, Seln, Oryn, Vastin, Pike, Teague, Hesk, Ostrand, Denvash, Lowmarch, Millrace and Treswick; Cleon is plan-required at the spring close (`manuscript/chapter-18.md:219–225`; `BOOK_MAP.md:395`). The shoulder factor, hold woman, broker, clerk, mule and Oryn's remembered city remain unnamed (`manuscript/chapter-14.md:59–105`; `manuscript/chapter-19.md:33–53`; `packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:8`).
+- The movement meets Reader Standard after the factual repairs: syntax and causal explanations are accessible; injury description is restrained; the fight's objective, positions, changed decision and cost are legible (`manuscript/chapter-14.md:109–249`; `manuscript/chapter-15.md:1–229`).
+- Sweep probe **2% skeleton / 15% close** is not by itself a copying finding (`AUTHOR-REPORT.md:36`). Direct protected/plan quotation is approximately 500–600 words—under two percent of the 33,942-word movement—counting the units enumerated in §5; the higher close score in chapters 18–19 is chiefly tracking narration in Cael/Seln's recurring catalogue-and-count cadence around the required spring/fork dialogue (`AUTHOR-REPORT.md:20,35–36`; `manuscript/chapter-18.md:1–225`; `manuscript/chapter-19.md:1–219`). The six literal markers account for about 150 non-prose words in the author's metric and disappear when fixed (`AUTHOR-REPORT.md:22,62–69`).
