+78. `manuscript/chapter-19.md`
+   old: `"There's a thing that none of you has asked me in two hundred and eighty days, and I've been glad of it. I'll say it once, since it bears on what I want of him." She did not look at Cael. "I wasn't made out here. I was made in a city, inside the Line. It doesn't matter which; they're all one city, with different rivers. There was a house there for the sick, with forty beds and six of us to tend them, and I'd my rank from it."`
+   new: `"There's a thing that none of you has asked me in two hundred and eighty days, and I've been glad of it. I'll say it once, since it bears on what I want of him." She did not look at Cael. "I wasn't made out here. I was certified in a city, inside the Line. It doesn't matter which; they're all one city, with different rivers. I healed for a year inside walls, and I'd my rank from it."`
+
+79. `manuscript/chapter-19.md`
+   old: `"Provisional. I never stayed to have it made anything else." She rubbed her palms together slowly. "Every bed in that house had a sheet on a board at its foot. There was the name on it, and the complaint, and what had been spent. And there was a column for the patient's tier."`
+   new: `"Provisional. I never stayed to have it made anything else." She rubbed her palms together slowly. "The walls had a ledger. There was the name, and the complaint, and what had been spent. And there was a column for the patient's tier."`
+
+80. `manuscript/chapter-19.md`
+   old: `"Not for the healer's. For theirs. I filled that column in for a long while before I asked what it was for; I thought that it was like the name. Then there was a week of fever in the low town, and the house was full to the stairs, and I found out." She spoke as she spoke a finding. "We'd so much in us, the six of us together, as I've so much in me tonight, and it had to be spent on somebody. It went down the column from the top. There was a Gold in a bed by the window with a wrenched wrist. He had what he wanted on the first day. Then the Silvers had theirs."`
+   new: `"Not for the healer's. For theirs. Bronze and above first. They told me that on the first day as if it were a kindness, as if I ought to be grateful not to be wasted on the yard." She spoke as she spoke a finding. "So I mended Bronzes with bruises while the people below the window waited."`
+
+81. `manuscript/chapter-19.md`
+   old: `"There was a woman brought in from the river sheds on the third night. She'd no tier that anybody could find. She'd never been stood on a plate, or her paper was lost; I never knew which. So there was nothing to put in the column." Oryn's eyes had gone to the peats. "A sheet with an empty column goes to the bottom of the heap. It's not cruelty. It's only how a heap is sorted."`
+   new: `"The yard went septic under the window while the ledger stayed correct." Oryn's eyes had gone to the peats. "It was not cruelty in any one line. It was only how the column sorted the work."`
+
+82. `manuscript/chapter-19.md`
+   old: `"Did she die?" said Lira, very low.`
+   new: `"So you left," said Lira, very low.`
+
+83. `manuscript/chapter-19.md`
+   old: `"She did not. I'll not have you think it worse than it was. I went to her at night, off the sheet, with what I had left, and it was enough. And in the morning the woman who kept that house showed me the board, where there was a spending and no tier written against it. She said that a healer who spends off the sheet has stolen from whoever stood next on it." Her spoon was in her hand, and she turned it over. "She was right. That's the thing that I've never got past. By that house's sums she was right, and I couldn't fault a line of them. So I went to look for some other sums."`
+   new: `"I walked out of a gate with my roll on my back and looked for some other sums." Her spoon was in her hand, and she turned it over. "The ledger was right by its own lines. I could not fault a line of it, and I could not stay under it."`
+
+84. `manuscript/chapter-19.md`
+   old: `"You left," said Cael.`
+   new: `Cael did not ask which city.`
+
+85. `manuscript/chapter-19.md`
+   old: `"I walked out of a gate in the coat that I stood in, and I've not been through one since."`
