+   new: `Oryn said, "You're whole. I can see it from here, and I said I'd read you when you'd slept a week and the ferry'd run, and you've slept a week and the ferry's run and I've not, because a road's not a table and I'll not read you at a fork with a city in front of you and a man's shoulder in the fire. That's on me. It's the one thing I'm walking up that road owing, and I'll pay it."`
+
+88. `manuscript/chapter-19.md`
+   old: `Brom unroped them himself. He had lashed them on the brown back at a ferry's shed with the beckets outward, so that they might go up any road; he had not said then that the last of that road would be on men's shoulders, and he did not say it now. He took the heaviest on his left side, where the webbing was not. Seln took the second by its beckets, on his back, above the strap of the case. The third stood on the frozen turf.`
