+90. `manuscript/chapter-19.md`
+   old: `There was not a great deal else to be done, since Karis had the flat under one arm and the hide under the other, as she had carried them off a landing. Lira took the tarred case in her left hand, by its strap, and nobody remarked on which hand it was. The healer's pannier stayed on the mule, with her linen in it, and a bow hung beside it with its one bolt.`
