+102. `manuscript/chapter-17.md`
+   old: `She had gone back to the uppermost row. She went through it a third time, quickly, looking only at the heads, and she laid a finger of her left glove on the rock for every group of four signs that she had not yet met in that row. The thumb went down last. She did the same with the second row, and the third, and so to the sixth, and each time the thumb went down, and no sixth finger was wanted.`
+   new: `She had gone back to the uppermost row. She went through it a third time, quickly, looking only at the heads, and made a pencil tick for every group of four signs that she had not yet met in that row. She did the same with the second row, and the third, and so to the sixth. The same number of ticks appeared each time, and she did not say the number.`

